{
  "title": "Ziyaarat-e-Naaheyah",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "Ziyaarat\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى آدَمَ صِفْوَةِ اللهِ مِنْ خَلِيْقَتِهٖ\nASSALAAMO A’LAA AADAMA SIFWATIL LAAHE MIN KHALEEQATEHI \nPeace be upon Adam, the chosen one of Allah from among His creation.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى شَيْثٍ وَلِيِّ اللهِ وَ خِيَرَتِهٖ\nASSALAAMO A’LAA SHEESA WALIYIL LAAHE WA KHEYARATEHI \nPeace be upon Seth (Shaith), the friend of Allah and His elite.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى اِدْرِيْسَ الْقائِمِ لِلّٰهِ بِحُجَّتِهٖ\nASSALAAMO A’LAA IDREESAL QAAEME LILLAAHE BE-HUJJATEHI \nPeace be upon Enoch (Idris), who established (religion) on behalf of Allah by His authority.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى نُوْحٍۨ الْمُجَابِ فِيْ دَعْوَتِهٖ\nASSALAAMO A’LAA NOOHENIL MOJAABE FEE DA’WATEHI\nPeace be upon Noah (Nuh), whose invocation (for punishment) was answered.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى هُوْدٍۨ الْمَمْدُوْدِ مِنَ اللهِ بِمَعُونَتِهٖ\nASSALAAMO A’LAA HOODENIL MAMDOODE MENAL LAAHE BE-MA-O’ONATEHI \nPeace be upon Hud, who was assisted through Allah’s aid.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى صَالِحِ الَّذِيْ تَوَّجَهُ اللهُ بِكَرامَتِهٖ\nASSALAAMO A’LAA SALEHENIL LAZEE TAWWAJAHUL LAAHO BE-KARAAMATEHI \nPeace be upon Salih, whom Allah crowned with His generosity.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى اِبْرَاهِيْمَ الَّذِيْ حَبَاهُ اللهُ بِخُلَّتِهٖ\nASSALAAMO A’LAA IBRAHIMAL LAZEE HABAAHUL LAAHO BE-KHULLATEHI\nPeace be upon Abraham (Ibrahim), whom Allah endowed with His friendship.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى اِسْمَاعِيْلَ الَّذِيْ فَدَاهُ اللهُ بِذِبْحٍ عَظِيْمٍ مِنْ جَنَّتِهٖ\nASSALAAMO A’LAA ISMAE’ELAL LAZEE FADAAHUL LAAHO BE-ZIBHIN A’ZEEMIM MIN JANNATEHI \nPeace be upon Ishmael (Isma’il), whom Allah ransomed with a great sacrifice from His Heaven.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى اِسْحَاقَ الَّذِيْ جَعَلَ اللهُ النُّبُوَّةَ فِيْ ذُرِّيَّتِهٖ\nASSALAAMO A’LAA ISHAAQAL LAZEE JAA’LAL LAAHUN NOBUWWATA FEE ZURRIYATEHI \nPeace be upon Isaac (Is’haq), in whose progeny Allah placed prophethood.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى يَعْقُوْبَ الَّذِيْ رَدَّ اللهُ عَلَيْهِ بَصَرَهٗ بِرَحْمَتِهٖ\nASSALAAMO A’LAA YA’QOOBAL LAZEE RADDAL LAAHO A’LAIHE BASARAHU BE-REHMATEHI \nPeace be upon Jacob (Ya’qub), for whom Allah restored his sight by His mercy.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى يُوْسُفَ الَّذِيْ نَجَّاهُ اللهُ مِنَ الْجُبِّ بِعَظَمَتِهٖ\nASSALAAMO A’LAA YUSUFAL LAZEE NAJAAHUL LAAHO MENAL JUBBE BE-A’ZAMATEHI\nPeace be upon Joseph (Yusuf), whom Allah rescued from the well by His majesty.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى مُوسَى الَّذِيْ فَلَقَ اللهُ الْبَحْرَ لَهٗ بِقُدْرَتِهٖ\nASSALAAMO A’LAA MUSAL LAZEE FALAQAL LAAHUL BAHRA LAHU BE-QUDRATEHI \nPeace be upon Moses (Musa), the one for whom Allah split the sea with His Power.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى هَارُوْنَ الَّذِيْ خَصَّهُ اللهُ بِنُبُوَّتِهٖ\nASSALAAMO A’LAA HAARUNAL LAZEE KHASSAHUL LAAHO BE-NOBUWWATEHI \nPeace be upon Aaron (Harun), whom Allah distinguished with his prophethood.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى شُعَيْبٍۨ الَّذِيْ نَصَرَهُ اللهُ عَلٰى اُمَّتِهٖ\nASSALAAMO A’LAA SHOA’IBENIL LAZEE NASARAHUL LAAHO A’LAA UMMATEHI \nPeace be upon Jethro (Shu’aib), whom Allah made victorious over his people.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى دَاوٗدَ الَّذِيْ تابَ اللهُ عَلَيْهِ مِنْ خَطِيْئَتِهٖ\nASSALAAMO A’LAA DAWOODAL LAZEE TAABAL LAAHO A’LAIHE MIN KHATEEATEHI\nPeace be upon Dawood, to whom Allah turned (in mercy) after his mistake.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى سُلَيْمَانَ الَّذِيْ ذَلَّتْ لَهٗ الْجِنُّ بِعِزَّتِهٖ\nASSALAAMO A’LAA SULAIMAANAL LAZEE ZALLAT LAHUL JINNO BE-I’ZZATEHI \nPeace be upon Sulaiman, for whom Allah made the Jinn subservient by His majesty.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى اَيُّوْبَ الَّذِيْ شَفاهُ اللهُ مِنْ عِلَّتِهٖ\nASSALAAMO A’LAA AYYOOBAL LAZEE SHAFAHUL LAAHO MIN I’LLATEHI \nPeace be upon Ayyub, whom Allah cured after his (prolonged) illness.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى يُوْنُسَ الَّذِيْ اَنْجَزَ اللهُ لَهٗ مَضْمُوْنَ عِدَتِهٖ\nASSALAAMO A’LAA YOONOSAL LAZEE ANJAZAL LAAHO MAZMOONA E’DATEHI \nPeace be upon Yunus, for whom Allah fulfilled the purport of His promise.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى عُزَيْرٍۨ الَّذِيْ اَحْيَاهُ اللهُ بَعْدَ مَيْتَتِهٖ\nASSALAAMO A’LAA OZAIRENIL LAZEE AHYAHUL LAAHO BA’DA MAYTATEHI\nPeace be upon Uzair, whom Allah brought to life after his death.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى زَكَرِيَّا الصَّابِرِ فِيْ مِحْنَتِهٖ\nASSALAAMO A’LAA ZAKARIYAS SAABERE FEE MEHNATEHI \nPeace be upon Zakariyya, who remained patient in his tribulations.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى يَحْيٰى الَّذِيْ اَزْلَفَهُ اللهُ بِشَهَادَتِهٖ\nASSALAAMO A’LAA YAHYAL LAZEE AZLAFAHUL LAAHO BE-SHAHADATEHI \nPeace be upon Yahya, whom Allah drew near (his rank) by his martyrdom.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى عِيْسٰى رُوْحِ اللهِ وَ كَلِمَتِهٖ\nASSALAAMO A’LAA E’ESAA RUHIL LAAHE WA KALEMATEHI\nPeace be upon Isa, the spirit of Allah and His word.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ حَبِيْبِ اللهِ وَ صِفْوَتِهٖ\nASSALAAMO A’LAA MOHAMMADIN HABEEBIL LAAHE WA SAFWATEHI \nPeace be upon Muhammad, the beloved of Allah and His elite.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى اَمِيْرِالْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ عَلِيِّ بْنِ اَبِيْ طَالِبٍ الْمَخْصُوْصِ بِاُخُوَّتِهٖ\nASSALAAMO A’LAA AMEERIL MOMINEENA A’LI IBNE ABI TAALEBENIL MAKHSOOSE BE-OKHOOWATEHI \nPeace be upon the Leader of the Faithful, Ali Ibn Abi Talib, who was exclusively selected for brotherhood to him (the Prophet (s.a.w.a.)).\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى فَاطِمَةَ الزَّهْرَاءِ ابْنَتِهٖ\nASSALAAMO A’LAA FAATEMATAZ ZAHRAAE IBNATEHI \nPeace be upon Fatima al-Zahra, his daughter.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى اَبِيْ مُحَمَّدٍۨ الْحَسَنِ وَصِيِّ اَبِيْهِ وَ خَلِيْفَتِهٖ\nASSALAAMO A’LAA ABI MOHAMMADENIL HASANE WASIYYE ABIHE WA KHALEEFATEHI \nPeace be upon Abu Muhammad al-Hasan, the executor of (the will of) his father, and his successor.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الْحُسَيْنِ الَّذِيْ سَمَحَتْ نَفْسُهٗ بِمُهْجَتِهٖ\nASSALAAMO A’LAL HUSAYNIL LAZEE SAMEHAT NAFSOHU BE-MOHJATEHI\nPeace be upon al-Husain, who sacrificed himself up to the last drops of the blood of his heart.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى مَنْ اَطَاعَ اللهَ فِيْ سِرِّهٖ وَ عَلانِيَتِهٖ\nASSALAAMO A’LAA MAN ATAA-A’L LAAHA FI SIRREHI WA A’LAANEYATEHI \nPeace be upon him, who obeyed Allah secretly and openly.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى مَنْ جَعَلَ اللهُ الشِّفَاءَ فِيْ تُرْبَتِهٖ\nASSALAAMO A’LAA MAN JOE’LASH SHEFAA-O FI TURBATEHI \nPeace be upon whom Allah placed a cure in the soil of his place (of martyrdom).\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى مَنِ الْاِجَابَةُ تَحْتَ قُبَّتِهٖ\nASSALAAMO A’LAA MANIL EJAABATO TAHTA QUBBATEHI \nPeace be upon the one under whose dome answer (to supplications) is guaranteed.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى مَنِ الْاَئِمَّةُ مِنْ ذُرِّيَّتِهٖ\nASSALAAMO A’LAA MANIL AI’MMATO MIN ZURRIYATEHI\nPeace be upon the one in whose descendants are the Imams (after him).\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى ابْنِ خاتَمِ الْاَنْبِيَاءِ\nASSALAAMO A’LA-BNE KHAATAMIL AMBIYAAE \nPeace be upon the son of the seal of the prophets.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى ابْنِ سَيِّدِ الْاَوْصِيَاءِ\nASSALAAMO A’LA-BNE SAYYEDIL AWSEYAAE \nPeace be upon the son of the chief of the executors.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى ابْنِ فَاطِمَةَ الزَّهْرَاءِ\nASSALAAMO A’LA-BNE FATEMATAZ ZAHRAAE \nPeace be upon the son of Fatima, the radiant.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى ابْنِ خَدِيْجَةَ الْكُبْرٰى\nASSALAAMO A’LA-BNE KHADIJATAL KUBRAA \nPeace be upon the son of Khadija, the great.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى ابْنِ سِدْرَةِ الْمُنْتَهٰى\nASSALAAMO A’LAA SIDRATIL MUNTAHA \nPeace be upon the son of the lote-tree in the outermost boundary (of Heaven).\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى ابْنِ جَنَّةِ الْمَأْوٰى\nASSALAAMO A’LA-BNE JANNATIL MAAWAA \nPeace be upon the son of the Garden of refuge.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى ابْنِ زَمْزَمَ وَ الصَّفَا\nASSALAAMO A’LA-BNE ZAMZAMA WAS SAFAA\nPeace be upon the son of Zamzam and al-Safaa.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الْمُرَمَّلِ بِالدِّمَاءِ\nASSALAAMO A’LAL MARAMMALE BIDDEMAAE \nPeace be upon him, who was saturated in (his) blood.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الْمَهْتُوْكِ الْخِبَاءِ\nASSALAAMO A’LAL MAHTOOKIL KHEBAAE \nPeace be upon him, whose tents were violated.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى خَامِسِ اَصْحابِ الْكِسَاءِ\nASSALAAMO A’LAA KHAAMESE ASHAABE AHLIL KISAAE \nPeace be upon the fifth of the People of the Cloak.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى غَرِيْبِ الْغُرَبَاءِ\nASSALAAMO A’LAA GHARIBIL GHORABAAE \nPeace be upon the loneliest of the lonely.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى شَهِيْدِ الشُّهَدَاءِ\nASSALAAMO A’LAA SHAHEEDISH SHOHADAAE \nPeace be upon the (greatest) martyr of all martyrs.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى قَتِيْلِ الْاَدْعِيَاءِ\nASSALAAMO A’LAA QATEELIL AD-E’YAAE \nPeace be upon him, who was slain by the individuals of illegitimate birth.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى سَاكِنِ كَرْبَلَاءَ\nASSALAAMO A’LAA SAAKENE KARBALAAE\nPeace be upon the one who is at rest in Karbala.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى مَنْ بَكَتْهُ مَلَائِكَةُ السَّمَاءِ\nASSALAAMO A’LAA MAN BAKATHO MALAEKATUS SAMAAE \nPeace be upon the one for whom the heavenly Angels wept.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى مَنْ ذُرِّيَّتُهُ الْاَزْكِيَاءُ\nASSALAAMO A’LAA MAN ZURRIYATOHUL AZKEYAAO \nPeace be upon the one whose descendants are the pure.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى يَعْسُوْبِ الدِّيْنِ\nASSALAAMO A’LAA YA’SOOBID DEEN \nPeace be upon the chief of the religion.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى مَنازِلِ الْبَرَاهِيْنِ\nASSALAAMO A’LAA MANAAZELIL BARAAHEEN \nPeace be upon the places of the (divine) proofs.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الْاَئِمَّةِ السَّادَاتِ\nASSALAAMO A’LAL AI’MMATIS SAADAATE \nPeace be upon the Imams, the masters (of mankind).\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الْجُيُوْبِ الْمُضَرَّجَاتِ\nASSALAAMO A’LAL JUYOOBIL MOZARRAJAATE \nPeace be upon the bloodstained chests.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الشِّفَاهِ الذَّابِلَاتِ\nASSALAAMO A’LASH SHEFAHIZ ZAABELAATE\nPeace be upon the parched lips.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى النُّفُوْسِ الْمُصْطَلَمَاتِ\nASSALAAMO A’LAN NOFOOSIL MUSTALEMAATE \nPeace be upon the plucked souls.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الْاَرْوَاحِ الْمُخْتَلَسَاتِ\nASSALAAMO A’LAL ARWAHIL MUKHTALESAATE \nPeace be upon the snatched spirits.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الْاَجْسَادِ الْعَارِيَاتِ\nASSALAAMO A’LAL AJSAADIL A’AREYAATE \nPeace be upon the stripped corpses.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الْجُسُوْمِ الشَّاحِبَاتِ\nASSALAAMO A’LAL JUSOOMISH SHAAHEBAATE\nPeace be upon the pallid bodies.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الدِّمَاءِ السَّائِلَاتِ\nASSALAAMO A’LAD DEMAAIS SAAELAATE \nPeace be upon the gushing bloods.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الْاَعْضَاءِ الْمُقَطَّعَاتِ\nASSALAAMO A’LAL AA’ZAAIL MUQATTA-AA’TE \nPeace be upon the dismembered limbs.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الرُّؤُوْسِ الْمُشَالَاتِ\nASSALAAMO A’LAR RO-OOSIL MOSHAALAATE \nPeace be upon the heads raised upon lances.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى النِّسْوَةِ الْبَارِزَاتِ\nASSALAAMO A’LAN NISWATIL BAAREZAATE\nPeace be upon the women (forcibly) exposed.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى حُجَّةِ رَبِّ الْعَالَمِيْنَ\nASSALAAMO A’LAA HUJJATE RABBIL A’ALAMEENA \nPeace be upon the Proof of the Lord of the worlds.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ وَ عَلٰى آبَائِكَ الطَّاهِرِيْنَ\nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA WA A’LAA AABAAEKAT TAAHEREEN \nPeace be upon you and upon your pure ancestors.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ وَ عَلٰى اَبْنَائِكَ الْمُسْتَشْهَدِيْنَ\nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA WA A’LAA ABNAAEKAL MUSTASHHADEENA \nPeace be upon you and upon your martyred sons.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ وَ عَلٰى ذُرِّيَّتِكَ النَّاصِرِيْنَ\nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA WA A’LAA ZURRIYATEKAN NAASEREENA \nPeace be upon you and upon your children who aided (you).\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ وَ عَلَى الْمَلَائِكَةِ الْمُضَاجِعِيْنَ\nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA WA A’LAL MALAAEKATIL MUZAAJEI’N\nPeace be upon you and upon the accompanying Angels.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الْقَتِيْلِ الْمَظْلُوْمِ\nASSALAAMO A’LAL QATEELIL MAZLOOME \nPeace be upon the slain and the oppressed one.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى اَخِيْهِ الْمَسْمُوْمِ\nASSALAAMO A’LAA AKHEEHIL MASMOOME \nPeace be upon his poisoned brother (Imam al-Hasan).\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى عَلِيٍّ الْكَبِيْرِ\nASSALAAMO A’LAA A’LIYYENIL KABEERE \nPeace be upon Ali, the elder (Ali al-Akbar).\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الرَّضِيْعِ الصَّغِيْرِ\nASSALAAMO A’LAR RAZEEIS SAGHEERE\nPeace be upon the suckling infant (Ali al-Asghar).\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الْاَبْدَانِ السَّلِيْبَةِ\nASSALAAMO A’LAL ABDAANIS SALEEBATE \nPeace be upon the plundered bodies.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الْعِتْرَةِ الْقَرِيْبَةِ [الْغَرِيْبَةِ]\nASSALAAMO A’LAL ITRATIL QAREEBATE \nPeace be upon the family and children who were nearby (the place of martyrdom) [who were without support among strangers].\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الْمُجَدَّلِيْنَ فِي الْفَلَوَاتِ\nASSALAAMO A’LAL MIJDALEEENA FIL FALAWAATE \nPeace be upon the mangled corpses (left) in the desert.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى النَّازِحِيْنَ عَنِ الْاَوْطَانِ\nASSALAAMO A’LAN NAAZEHEENA A’NIL AWTAANE\nPeace be upon those who were left far from their homeland.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الْمَدْفُوْنِيْنَ بِلَا اَكْفَانِ\nASSALAAMO A’LAL MADFUNEENA BELAA AKFAANE \nPeace be upon those who were buried without shrouds.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الرُّؤُوْسِ الْمُفَرَّقَةِ عَنِ الْاَبْدَانِ\nASSALAAMO A’LAR RO-OOSIL MUFARRAQATE A’NIL ABDAANE \nPeace be upon the heads severed from the bodies.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الْمُحْتَسِبِ الصَّابِرِ\nASSALAAMO A’LAL MOHTASEBIS SAABERE\nPeace be upon the bereaved and the patient one.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الْمَظْلُوْمِ بِلَا نَاصِرٍ\nASSALAAMO A’LAL MAZLOOME BELA NAASEREEN \nPeace be upon the oppressed one who was without a helper.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى سَاكِنِ التُّرْبَةِ الزَّاكِيَةِ\nASSALAAMO A’LAA SAAKENIT TURBATIZ ZAAKEYATE \nPeace be upon the inhabitant of the purified soil.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى صَاحِبِ الْقُبَّةِ السَّامِيَةِ\nASSALAAMO A’LAA SAAHEBIL QUBBATIS SAAMEYATE \nPeace be upon the possessor of the lofty dome.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى مَنْ طَهَّرَهُ الْجَلِيْلُ\nASSALAAMO A’LAA MAN TAHHARAHUL JALEELO \nPeace be upon him, whom the Almighty purified.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى مَنِ افْتَخَرَ بِهٖ جَبْرَئِيْلُ\nASSALAAMO A’LAA MANIF TAKHARA BEHI JIBRAEELO \nPeace be upon him, of whom Gabriel (Jabra’il) was proud.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى مَنْ نَاغَاهُ فِي الْمَهْدِ مِيْكَائِيْلُ\nASSALAAMO A’LAA MAN NAAGHAAHO FIL MAHDE MIKAAEELO\nPeace be upon the one to whom Michael (Mika’il) spoke tenderly in the cradle.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى مَنْ نُكِثَتْ ذِمَّتُهٗ\nASSALAAMO A’LAA MAN NOKESAT ZIMMATOHU \nPeace be upon the one whose pact was broken.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى مَنْ هُتِكَتْ حُرْمَتُهٗ\nASSALAAMO A’LAA MAN HOTEKAT HURMATOHU \nPeace be upon the one whose rights and dignity were violated.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى مَنْ اُرِيْقَ بِالظُّلْمِ دَمُهٗ\nASSALAAMO A’LAA MAN OREEQA BIZZULME DAMOHU \nPeace be upon the one whose blood was shed unjustly.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الْمُغَسَّلِ بِدَمِ الْجِرَاحِ\nASSALAAMO A’LAL MUGHASSALE BEDAMIL JORAAHE \nPeace be upon the one who was bathed in the blood of his wounds.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الْمُجَرَّعِ بِكَأْسَاتِ الرِّمَاحِ\nASSALAAMO A’LAL MUJADDAE’ BE-KAASAATIR REMAAHE\nPeace be upon the one who tasted the spears raining down over his body.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الْمُضَامِ الْمُسْتَبَاحِ\nASSALAAMO A’LAL MUZAAMIL MUSTABAAHE\nPeace be upon the one against whom people came together and made lawful the shedding of his blood.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الْمَنْحُوْرِ فِي الْوَرٰى\nASSALAAMO A’LAL MANHOORE FIL WARAA \nPeace be upon the one slaughtered in public.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى مَنْ دَفَنَهٗ اَهْلُ الْقُرٰى\nASSALAAMO A’LAA MAN DAFANAHU AHLUL QORAA \nPeace be upon the one who was buried by the strangers from (nearby) villages.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الْمَقْطُوعِ الْوَتِيْنِ\nASSALAAMO A’LAL MAQTUI’L WATEENE \nPeace be upon the one whose aorta was severed.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الْمُحَامِيْ بِلَا مُعِيْنِ\nASSALAAMO A’LAL MUHAAMAA BELAA MOE’ENE\nPeace be upon the defender who had no helper.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الشَّيْبِ الْخَضِيْبِ\nASSALAAMO A’LASH SHAYBIL KHAZEEBE\nPeace be upon the grey hair that was dyed (with blood).\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الْخَدِّ التَّرِيْبِ\nASSALAAMO A’LAL KHADDIT TAREEBE\nPeace be upon the cheek that struck the dust.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الْبَدَنِ السَّلِيْبِ\nASSALAAMO A’LAL BADANIS SALEEBE \nPeace be upon the butchered body.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الثَّغْرِ الْمَقْرُوْعِ بِالْقَضِيْبِ\nASSALAAMO A’LAS SAGHRIL MAQRUE’ BIL QAZEEBE \nPeace be upon the front teeth that were beaten with a rod.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الرَّأْسِ الْمَرْفُوْعِ\nASSALAAMO A’LAR RAASIL MARFOOE’ \nPeace be upon the head raised (upon a lance).\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الْاَجْسَامِ الْعَارِيَةِ فِي الْفَلَوَاتِ \nASSALAAMO A’LAL AJSAAMIL A’AREYATE FIL FALAWAATE \nPeace be upon the unclothed corpses in the desert, \nتَنْهَشُهَا الذِّئَابُ الْعَادِيَاتُ \nTANHASHOHAAZ ZEAABUL A’ADEYAATO \nbitten by wild wolves \nوَ تَخْتَلِفُ اِلَيْهَا السِّبَاعُ الضَّارِيَاتُ\nWA TAKHTALEFO ELAYHAS SEBAAU’Z ZAAREYAATO\nand around whom the beasts of prey prowled.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يا مَوْلَايَ وَ عَلَى الْمَلَائِكَةِ الْمَرْفُوْفِيْنَ حَوْلَ قُبَّتِكَ\nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YAA MAWLAAYA WA A’LAL MALAAAEKATIL MARFOOFEENA HAULA QUBBATEKAL \nPeace be upon you, O my master, and the Angels who flutter around your dome,\nالْحَافِّيْنَ بِتُرْبَتِكَ الطَّائِفِيْنَ بِعَرْصَتِكَ الْوَارِدِيْنَ لِزِيَارَتِكَ\nHAAFFEENA BE-TURBATEKAT TAAEFEENA BE-A’RSATEKAL WAAREDEENA LE-ZEYAARATEKA \nsurround your grave, circumambulate your courtyard, and come for your visitation.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ فَاِنِّيْ قَصَدْتُ اِلَيْكَ وَ رَجَوْتُ الْفَوْزَ لَدَيْكَ\nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA FA INNEE QASADTO ELAYKA WA RAJAWTUL FAUZA LADAYKA\nPeace be upon you! Indeed, I intended your visitation, and I am hopeful of achieving the prosperity that is with you.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ\nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA \nSalutations to you,\nسَلَامَ الْعَارِفِ بِحُرْمَتِكَ الْمُخْلِصِ فِيْ وِلَايَتِكَ الْمُتَقَرِّبِ اِلَى اللهِ بِمَحَبَّتِكَ الْبَرِيْءِ مِنْ اَعْدَائِكَ\nSALAAMAL A’AREFE BE-HURMATEKAL MUKHLESE FEE WELAAYATEKAL MOTAQARREBE ILALLAHE BE-MAHABBATEKAL BAREE-E MIN AA’DAAEKA \nSalutations from he who recognizes your sanctity, is a sincere (believer) in your guardianship, seeks nearness to Allah through your love, and is aloof from your enemies,\nسَلَامَ مَنْ قَلْبُهٗ بِمُصَابِكَ مَقْرُوْحٌ \nSALAAMA MAN QALBOHU BEMOSAABEKA MAQRUHUN \nSalutations from the one whose heart is wounded due to the tribulations you have suffered, \nوَ دَمْعُهٗ عِنْدَ ذِكْرِكَ مَسْفُوْحٌ\nWA DAM-O’HU I’NDA ZIKREKA MASFOOHUN \nand whose tears flow in your remembrance,\nسَلَامَ الْمَفْجُوعِ الْحَزِيْنِ الْوَالِهِ الْمُسْتَكِيْنِ\nSALAAMAL MAZJOOI’L HAZEENIL WAALEHIL MUSTAKEENE\nSalutations from the one who is distressed, grief-stricken, distracted, and yielding,\nسَلَامَ مَنْ لَوْ كَانَ مَعَكَ بِالطُّفُوْفِ \nSALAAMA MAN LAW KAANA MA-A’KA BITTOFOOFE \nSalutations from the one, who, had he been present with you in that plain, \nلَوَقَاكَ بِنَفْسِهٖ حَدَّ السُّيُوْفِ \nLAWAQAAKA BENAFSEHI HADDAS SOYOOFE\nwould have shielded you from the sharpness of the swords with his body \nوَ بَذَلَ حُشَاشَتَهٗ دُوْنَكَ لِلْحُتُوْفِ\nWA BAZALA HOSHAASHATAHU DOONAKA LIL-HOTOOFE \nand sacrificed his last breath for you,\nوَ جَاهَدَ بَيْنَ يَدَيْكَ وَ نَصَرَكَ عَلٰى مَنْ بَغٰى عَلَيْكَ وَ فَدَاكَ بِرُوْحِهٖ وَ جَسَدِهٖ وَ مَالِهٖ وَ وَلَدِهٖ\nWA JAAHADA BAYNA YADAYKA WA NASARAKA A’LAA MAN BAGHAA A’LAYKA WA FADAAKA BE-ROOHEHI WA JASADEHI WA MAALEHI WA WALADEHI \nwould have struggled beside you, helped you against the aggressors, and redeemed you with his soul, body, wealth, and children,\nوَ رُوْحُهٗ لِرُوْحِكَ فِدَاءٌ\nWA ROOHOHU LEROOHEKA FEDAAUN \n(Salutations from the one) whose soul is a sacrifice for yours,\nوَ اَهْلُهٗ لِاَهْلِكَ وِقَاءٌ\nWA AHLOHU LE-AHLEKA WEQAAUN \nand whose family is a shield for yours.\nفَلَئِنْ اَخَّرَتْنِي الدُّهُوْرُ وَ عَاقَنِيْ عَنْ نَصْرِكَ الْمَقْدُوْرُ\nFALAIN AKKHARAT-NID DOHOORO WA A’AQANEE A’N NASREKAL MAQDOORO \nBut as I have been hindered by the course of time and as (Allah’s) decree has prevented me from helping you,\nوَ لَمْ اَكُنْ لِمَنْ حارَبَكَ مُحَارِبًا وَ لِمَنْ نَصَبَ لَكَ الْعَدَاوَةَ مُناصِبًا\nWA LAM AKUN LEMAN HAARABAKA MOHAAREBAN WA LEMAN NASABA LAKAL A’DAAWATA MONAASEBAN \nand as I could not fight those who fought you, and was not able to show hostility to those who showed hostility to you, \nفَلَاَنْدُبَنَّكَ صَبَاحًا وَ مَسَاءً وَ لَاَبْكِيَنَّ لَكَ بَدَلَ الدُّمُوْعِ دَمًا حَسْرَةً عَلَيْكَ وَ تَاَسُّفًا عَلٰى مَا دَهَاكَ وَ تَلَهُّفًا\nFALA ANDOBANNAKA SABAAHAN WA MASAA-AN WA LA-ABKEYANNA LAKA BADALAD DOMUE’ DAMAN HASRATAN A’LAYKA WA TA-ASSOFAN A’LAA MAA DAHAAKA WA TALAHHOFAN \nI will, therefore, lament you morning and evening, and will weep blood in place of tears, out of my anguish for you and my sorrow for all that befell you,\nحَتّٰى اَمُوْتَ بِلَوْعَةِ الْمُصَابِ وَ غُصَّةِ الْاِكْتِيَابِ\nHATTAA AMOOTA BE-LAUA’TIL MOSAABE WA GHUSSATIL IKTEYAABE\nuntil I meet death from the pain of the catastrophe and the choking grief.\nاَشْهَدُ اَ نَّكَ قَدْ اَقَمْتَ الصَّلٰوةَ وَ اٰتَيْتَ الزَّكٰوةَ\nASH-HADO ANNAKA QAD AQAMTAS SALAATA WA AATAYTAZ ZAKAATA \nI bear witness that you certainly established prayer, gave alms,\nوَ اَمَرْتَ بِالْمَعْرُوْفِ وَ نَهَيْتَ عَنِ الْمُنْكَرِ وَ الْعُدْوَانِ\nWA AMARTA BIL-MA’ROOFE WA NAHAYTA A’NIL MUNKARE WAL UDWAANE \nenjoined good, forbade evil and transgression,\nوَ اَطَعْتَ اللهَ وَ مَا عَصَيْتَهٗ وَ تَمَسَّكْتَ بِهٖ وَ بِحَبْلِهٖ \nWA ATA’TAL LAAHA WA MAA A’SAYTAHU WA TAMASSAKTA BEHI WA BE-HABLEHI\nobeyed Allah, never disobeyed Him, and held fast to Him and to His rope.\nفَاَرْضَيْتَهٗ وَ خَشَيْتَهٗ وَ رَاقَبْتَهٗ وَ اسْتَجَبْتَهٗ\nFA-ARZAYTAHU WA KHASHAYTAHU WA RAAQABTAHU WAS TAJABTAHU\nThen, you pleased Him, held Him in awe, were attentive towards Him, and were responsive to Him,\nوَ سَنَنْتَ السُّنَنَ وَ اَطْفَأْتَ الْفِتَنَ\nWA SANANTAS SONANA WA ATFAATAL FETANA \nestablished the customs (of the Prophet (s.a.w.a.)), extinguished turmoil (in religion),\nوَ دَعَوْتَ اِلَى الرَّشَادِ وَ اَوْضَحْتَ سُبُلَ السَّدَادِ وَ جَاهَدْتَ فِي اللهِ حَقَّ الْجِهَادِ\nWA DA-A’WTA ELAR RESHAADE WA AWZAHTA SOBOLAS SEDAADE WA JAAHADTA FILLAAHE HAQQAL JEHAADE \ninvited people to rectitude, clarified the ways of righteousness, and truly strove in the way of Allah.\nوَ كُنْتَ لِلّٰهِ طَائِعًا\nWA KUNTA LILLAAHE TAAEA’N \nYou were an obedient one to Allah, \nوَ لِجَدِّكَ مُحَمَّدٍ صَلَّى اللهُ عَلَيْهِ وَ اٰلِهٖ تَابِعًا\nWA LEJADDEKA MOHAMMADIN SALLAL LAAHO A’LAYHE WA AALEHI TAABEA’N \na follower of your grandfather, Muhammad, peace be upon him and his family, \nوَ لِقَوْلِ اَبِيْكَ سَامِعًا\nWA LE-QAULE ABEEKA SAAMEA’N \nheedful of the saying of your father,\nوَ اِلٰى وَصِيَّةِ اَخِيْكَ مُسَارِعًا\nWA ELA WASIYYATE AKHEEKA MOSAAREA’N \nquick to execute the will of your brother,\nوَ لِعِمَادِ الدِّيْنِ رَافِعًا وَ لِلطُّغْيَانِ قَامِعًا\nWA LE-E’MAADIDDEENE RAAFEA’N WA LIT-TUGHYAANE QAAME-A’N \nan erector of the pillars of the religion, a suppressor of tyranny,\nوَ لِلطُّغَاةِ مُقَارِعًا وَ لِلْاُمَّةِ نَاصِحًا\nWA LIT-TOGHAATE MOQAAREAN WA LIL-UMMATE NAASEHAN\nan advancer on the transgressors, and a sincere exhorter for the nation,\nوَ فِيْ غَمَرَاتِ الْمَوْتِ سَابِحًا\nWA FEE GHAMARAATIL MAWTE SAABEHAN \na traveler into mortal throes,\nوَ لِلْفُسَّاقِ مُكَافِحًا وَ بِحُجَجِ اللهِ قَائِمًا\nWA LIL-FUSSAAQE MUKAAFEHAN WA BE-HOJJAJIL LAAHE QAAEMAN \na warrior against the wretched, and a maintainer of Allah’s proofs (on earth),\nوَ لِلْاِسْلَامِ وَ الْمُسْلِمِيْنَ رَاحِمًا\nWA LIL-ISLAAME WAL MUSLEMEENA RAAHEMAN \ncompassionate towards Islam and Muslims,\nوَ لِلْحَقِّ نَاصِرًا وَ عِنْدَ الْبَلَاءِ صَابِرًا\nWA LIL-HAQQE NAASERAN WA INDAL BALAAE SAABERAN \na champion of truth and most patient in adversity,\nوَ لِلدِّيْنِ كَالِئًا وَ عَنْ حَوْزَتِهٖ مُرَامِيًا\nWA LIDDEENE KAALEAN WA A’N HAUZATEHI MORAAMEYAN\na protector for the religion, and a defender of its domain.\nتَحُوْطُ الْهُدٰى وَ تَنْصُرُهٗ\nTAHOOTUL HODAA WA TANSOROHU \nYou safeguarded the right path and supported it, \nوَ تَبْسُطُ الْعَدْلَ وَ تَنْشُرُهٗ\nWA TABSOTUL A’DLA WA TANSHOROHU \nspread justice and promoted it, \nوَ تَنْصُرُ الدِّيْنَ وَ تُظْهِرُهٗ\nWA TANSORUDDEENA WA TUZHEROHU \nadvocated the faith and manifested it,\nوَ تَكُفُّ الْعَابِثَ وَ تَزْجُرُهٗ\nWA TAKUFFUL A’ABESA WA TAZJOROHU \nrestrained and reproached the frivolous, \nوَ تَأْخُذُ لِلدَّنِيِّ مِنَ الشَّرِيْفِ\nWA TAA-KHOZO LIDDANIYYE MENASH SHAREEFE \ntook back (the rights) of the lowly from the privileged, \nوَ تُسَاوٰي فِي الْحُكْمِ بَيْنَ الْقَوِيِّ وَ الضَّعِيْفِ\nWA TOSAAWI FIL HUKME BAYNAL QAWWIYYE WAZ ZAE’EFE \nand were equitable in your arbitrations between the weak and the strong.\nكُنْتَ رَبِيْعَ الْاَيْتَامِ وَ عِصْمَةَ الْاَنَامِ وَ عِزَّ الْاِسْلَامِ\nKUNTA RABIA’L AYTAAME, WA I’SMATAL ANAAME WA I’ZZAL ISLAAME \nYou were the springtime of the orphans, the protection of humanity, the glory of Islam, \nوَ مَعْدِنَ الْاَحْكَامِ وَ حَلِيْفَ الْاِنْعَامِ\nWA MA’DENAL AHKAAME WA HALEEFAL INA’AME \nthe treasure of divine laws, and a relentless ally of benevolence. \nسَالِكًا طَرَائِقَ [فِيْ طَرِيْقَةِ] جَدِّكَ وَ اَبِيْكَ\nSAALEKAN TARAAEQA (FEE TAREEQATE) JADDEKA WA ABEEKA \nYou pursued the path of your grandfather and your father,\nمُشْبِهًا فِي الْوَصِيَّةِ لِاَخِيْكَ\nMUSHBEHAN FIL WASIYYATE LE-AKHEEKA\nresembled your brother in will,\nوَفِيَّ الذِّمَمِ رَضِيَّ الشِّيَمِ\nWA FIYYAZ ZEMAME RAZIYYASH SHEYAME \nwere loyal to your obligations, possessed pleasant manners,\nظَاهِرَ الْكَرَمِ مُتَهَجِّدًا فِي الظُّلَمِ\nZAAHERAL KARAME MOTAHAJJEDAN FIZZOLAME \nembodied generosity, and spent the darkness (of night) in prayer.\nقَوِيْمَ الطَّرَائِقِ كَرِيْمَ الْخَلَائِقِ عَظِيْمَ السَّوَابِقِ\nQAWEEMAT TARAAEQE KARIMAL KHALAAEQE A’ZEEMAS SAWAABEQE \nYou were the straightest path, the most generous of the creation, and had the brightest record.\nشَرِيْفَ النَّسَبِ مُنِيْفَ الْحَسَبِ رَفِيْعَ الرُّتَبِ\nSHAREEFAN NASABE MONIFAL HASABE RAFI-A’R ROTABE \nYou were of great ancestry, noble descent, and lofty rank.\nكَثِيْرَ الْمَنَاقِبِ مَحْمُوْدَ الضَّرَائِبِ جَزِيْلَ الْمَوَاهِبِ\nKASEERAL MANAAQEBE MAHMOODAZ ZARAA-EBE JAZEELAL MAWAAHEBE \nYou possessed plentiful merits, praiseworthy manners, and were abundant in endowments.\nحَلِيْمٌ رَشِيْدٌ مُنِيْبٌ جَوَادٌ عَلِيْمٌ شَدِيْدٌ\nHALEEMUR RASHIDUN MUNEEBUN JAWAADUN A’LEEMUN SHADEEDUN \nYou were forbearing, upright, always turning (to Allah), generous, knowledgeable, strong, \nاِمَامٌ شَهِيْدٌ اَوَّاهٌ مُنِيْبٌ حَبِيْبٌ مَهِيْبٌ\nEMAAMUN SHAHEEDUN AWWAAHUN MONEEBUN HABEEBUN MAHEEBUN\na martyred Imam, grieved, repentant with earnest prayers (to Allah), dearly loved, and awesome.\nكُنْتَ لِلرَّسُولِ صَلَّى اللهُ عَلَيْهِ وَ اٰلِهٖ وَلَدًا\nKUNTA LIR RASOOLE SALLAL LAAHO A’LAYHE WA AALEHI WALADAN \nYou were to the Messenger, peace be upon him and his family, a son,\nوَ لِلْقُرْآنِ سَنَدًا [مُنْقِذًا]\nWA LIL-QURAANE SANADAN (MUNQEZAN)\nfor the Quran, an authority [a savior],\nوَ لِلْاُمَّةِ عَضُدًا\nWA LIL-UMMATE A’ZODAN \nand for the nation, a support.\nوَ فِي الطَّاعَةِ مُجْتَهِدًا\nWA FITTAA-A’TE MUJTAHEDAN \nYou were diligent in obedience,\nحَافِظًا لِلْعَهْدِ وَ الْمِيْثَاقِ\nHAAFEZAN LIL-A’HDE WAL MEESAAQE \na protector of the covenant and oath,\nنَاكِبًا عَنْ سُبُلِ الْفُسَّاقِ\nNAAKEBAN A’N SOBOLIL FUSSAAQE \nkeeping away from the paths of the debauched,\n[وَ] بَاذِلًا لِلْمَجْهُوْدِ\n(WA) BAAZELAN LIL-MAJHOODE \nsparing no effort (in fulfilling the duties),\nطَوِيْلَ الرُّكُوْعِ وَ السُّجُوْدِ\nTAWEELAR ROKOOE’ WAS SOJOODE\nperforming prolonged bowing and prostrations,\nزَاهِدًا فِي الدُّنْيَا زُهْدَ الرَّاحِلِ عَنْهَا\nZAAHEDAN FIDDUNYA ZOHDAR RAAHELE A’NHA \nabstaining from the world, like one who is departing from it,\nنَاظِرًا اِلَيْهَا بِعَيْنِ الْمُسْتَوْحِشِيْنَ مِنْهَا\nNAAZERAN ELAIHAA BE-A’YNIL MUSTAUHESHEENA MINHA \nlooking upon it (the world) through the eyes of one estranged (from it).\nآمَالُكَ عَنْهَا مَكْفُوْفَةٌ\nAAMAALOKA A’NHAA MAKFOOFATUN \nYour desires from it (the world) were abstentious,\nوَ هِمَّتُكَ عَنْ زِيْنَتِهَا مَصْرُوْفَةٌ\nWA HIMMATOKA A’N ZEENATEHA MASROOFATUN \nyour efforts were far-removed from its embellishments,\nوَ اَلْحَاظُكَ عَنْ بَهْجَتِهَا مَطْرُوْفَةٌ\nWA ALHAA’ZOKA A’N BAHJATEHA MATRUFATUN \nyour glances removed from its joys,\nوَ رَغْبَتُكَ فِي الْآخِرَةِ مَعْرُوْفَةٌ\nWA RAGHBATOKA FIL AAKHERATE MA’RUFATUN \nand your desire for the hereafter was well-known,\nحَتّٰى اِذَا الْجَوْرُ مَدَّ بَاعَهٗ\nHATTAA EZAL JAWRO MADDABAA-A’HU \neven when tyranny became wide-spread,\nوَ اَسْفَرَ الظُّلْمُ قِنَاعَهٗ\nWA ASFARAZ ZULMO QENAA-A’HU \ninjustice removed its veil,\nوَ دَعَا الْغَيُّ اَتْبَاعَهٗ\nWA DA-A’L GHAYYO ATBAA-A’HU \nwickedness called upon its followers,\nوَ اَنْتَ فِيْ حَرَمِ جَدِّكَ قاطِنٌ\nWA ANTA FEE HARAME JADDEKA QAATENUN \nand you were residing in the sanctuary of your grandfather,\nوَ لِلظَّالِمِيْنَ مُبَايِنٌ\nWA LIZ-ZAALEMEENA MOBAAYENUN \ndetached from the oppressors,\nجَلِيْسُ الْبَيْتِ وَ الْمِحْرَابِ\nJALEESUL BAYTE WAL-MEHRAABE \nsitting in the house and the prayer niche,\nمُعْتَزِلٌ عَنِ اللَّذَّاتِ وَ الشَّهَوَاتِ\nMO’TAZELUN A’NIL LAZZAATE WASH SHAHAWAATE \nunattached to (worldly) pleasures and carnal desires,\nتُنْكِرُ الْمُنْكَرَ بِقَلْبِكَ وَ لِسَانِكَ عَلٰى حَسَبِ طاقَتِكَ وَ اِمْكَانِكَ\nTUNKERUL MUNKARA BE-QALBEKA WA LESAANEKA A’LAA HASABE TAAQATEKA WA IMKAANEKA \nand renouncing evil in your heart and on your tongue to the extent of your strength and ability.\nثُمَّ اقْتَضَاكَ الْعِلْمُ لِلْاِنْكَارِ\nSUMMAQ TAZAAKAL I’LMO LIL-INKAARE \nThen the knowledge demanded you for disavowal (of falsehood),\nوَ لَزِمَكَ [اَلْزَمَكَ] اَنْ تُجَاهِدَ الْفُجَّارَ\nWA LAZEMAKA (ALZAMAKA) AN TOJAAHEDAL FUJJAARA \nand made it incumbent on you to struggle against the deviant.\nفَسِرْتَ فِيْ اَوْلَادِكَ وَ اَهَالِيْكَ وَ شِيْعَتِكَ وَ مَوَالِيْكَ\nFASIRTA FEE AWLAADEKA WA AHAALEEKA WA SHIA’TEKA WA MAWAALEEKA \nTherefore, you set out in company of your children, kinsfolk, followers, and supporters,\nوَ صَدَعْتَ بِالْحَقِّ وَ الْبَيِّنَةِ\nWA SADA’TA BIL-HAQQE WAL BAYYENATE \ndisclosed the truth and clear proofs,\nوَ دَعَوْتَ اِلَى اللهِ بِالْحِكْمَةِ وَ الْمَوْعِظَةِ الْحَسَنَةِ\nWA DA-A’WTA ILLAL LAAHE BIL-HIKMATE WAL MAWE’ZATIL HASANATE \nsummoned people towards Allah with wisdom and fine exhortation,\nوَ اَمَرْتَ بِاِقَامَةِ الْحُدُوْدِ وَ الطَّاعَةِ لِلْمَعْبُوْدِ\nWA AMARTA BE-EQAAMATIL HODOODE WAT TAA-A’TE LIL-MA’BOODE \nordered the establishment of the limits of divine law, and the obedience to the One Who should be worshipped,\nوَ نَهَيْتَ عَنِ الْخَبَائِثِ وَ الطُّغْيَانِ\nWA NAHAITA A’NIL KHABAAESE WAT TUGHYAANE \nand forbade (people) from wickedness and oppression.\nوَ وَاجَهُوْكَ بِالظُّلْمِ وَ الْعُدْوَانِ\nWA WAAJAHOOKA BIZ-ZULME WAL U’DWAANE\nBut, they confronted you with injustice and aggression.\nفَجَاهَدْتَهُمْ بَعْدَ الْاِيْعَازِ لَهُمْ [الْاِيْعَادِ اِلَيْهِمْ] وَ تَاْكِيْدِ الْحُجَّةِ عَلَيْهِمْ\nFAJAAHADTAHUM BA’DAL EE-A’AZE LAHUM (EE-A’ADE ELAYHIM) WA TAAKEEDIL HUJJATE A’LAIHIM \nTherefore, you resisted them after advising them and stressing over (divine) proofs against them.\nفَنَكَثُوْا ذِمَامَكَ وَ بَيْعَتَكَ\nFANAKASU ZEMAAMAKA WA BAY-A’TAKA \nHowever, they violated your (divine) rights and oath.\nوَ اَسْخَطُوْا رَبَّكَ وَ جَدَّكَ\nWA ASKHATOO RABBAKA WA JADDAKA \nangered your Lord and your grandfather,\nوَ بَدَؤُوْكَ بِالْحَرْبِ\nWA BADAOOKA BIL-HARBE \nand initiated battle against you.\nفَثَبَتَّ لِلطَّعْنِ وَ الضَّرْبِ\nFASABATTA LITTA’NE WAZ-ZARBE \nHence, you stood firm to spear and strike,\nوَ طَحَنْتَ جُنُوْدَ الْفُجَّارِ وَ اقْتَحَمْتَ قَسْطَلَ الْغُبَارِ\nWA TAHANTA JONOODAL FUJJAARE WAQTAHAMTA QASTALAL GHOBAARE \npulverized the soldiers of the transgressors, and stormed (courageously) into the dust of the battle,\nمُجَالِدًا بِذِىْ الْفَقَارِ كَاَنَّكَ عَلِيٌّ الْمُخْتَارُ\nMOJAADELAN BE-ZIL FEQAARE KA ANNAKA A’LIYYONIL MUKHTAARE\nfighting with Zulfiqar as if you were Ali, the chosen one.\nفَلَمَّا رَاَوْكَ ثَابِتَ الْجَاشِ غَيْرَ خَائِفٍ وَ لَا خَاشٍ\nFALAMMAA RA-AWKA SAABETAL JAASHE GHAIRA KHAA-EFIN WA LAA KHAASHIN \nSo when they saw you firm, fearless, and courageous,\nنَصَبُوْا لَكَ غَوَائِلَ مَكْرِهِمْ وَ قَاتَلُوْكَ بِكَيْدِهِمْ وَ شَرِّهِمْ\nNASABOO LAKA GAWAAELA MAKREHIM WA QAATALOOKA BE-KAIDEHIM WA SHARREHIM \nthey set up their most malicious deceptions against you, and fought you with their deceit and viciousness.\nوَ اَمَرَ اللَّعِيْنُ جُنُوْدَهٗ فَمَنَعُوْكَ الْمَاءَ وَ وُرُوْدَهٗ\nWA AMARAL LAE’ENO JONUDAHU FAMANO’OKAL MAA-A WA WOROODAHU \nThe accursed one (Umar Ibn Sa’d) commanded his soldiers, and thus, they prevented you from reaching or receiving water.\nوَ نَاجَزُوْكَ الْقِتَالَ وَ عَاجَلُوْكَ النِّزَالَ\nWA NAAJAZUKAL QETAALA WA A’AJALOOKAN NEZAALA \nThey rushed to engage you in combat, descended swiftly upon you,\nوَ رَشَقُوْكَ بِالسِّهَامِ وَ النِّبَالِ\nWA RASHAQOOKA BISSEHAAME WAN NEBAALE \nshowering you with arrows and stones,\nوَ بَسَطُوْا اِلَيْكَ اَكُفَّ الْاِصْطِلَامِ\nWA BASATOO ELAYKA AKUFFAL ISTELAAME\nand moving towards you with uprooting hands.\nوَ لَمْ يَرْعَوْا لَكَ ذِمَامًا وَ لَا رَاقَبُوْا فِيْكَ اَثَامًا فِيْ قَتْلِهِمْ اَوْلِيَائَكَ وَ نَهْبِهِمْ رِحَالَكَ\nWA LAM YAR-A’W LAKA ZEMAAMAN WA LAA RAAQABOO FEEKA AASAAMAN FEE QATLEHIM AWLEYAA-AKA WA NAHBEHIM REHAALAKA \nNeither they respected your rights, nor were they mindful of retribution for slaying you and your companions, and plundering your belongings.\nوَ اَنْتَ مُقَدَّمٌ فِي الْهَبَوَاتِ وَ مُحْتَمِلٌ لِلْاَذِيَّاتِ\nWA ANTA MUQDDAMUN FIL HABAWAATE WA MOHTAMELUN LIL-AZIYYAATE \nYou were in the front line of the storm (of battle), enduring afflictions.\nقَدْ عَجِبَتْ مِنْ صَبْرِكَ مَلَائِكَةُ السَّمَاوَاتِ\nQAD A’JEBAT MIN SABREKA MALAAAEKATUS SAMAAWAATE \nIndeed, the angels of the heavens were astonished by your patience.\nفَاَحْدَقُوْا بِكَ مِنْ كُلِّ الْجِهَاتِ\nFA-AHDAQOO BEKA MIN KULLIL JEHAATE \nThe enemy then surrounded you from all sides,\nوَ اَثْخَنُوْكَ بِالْجِرَاحِ\nASKHANUKA BIL-JERAAHE \nweakened you by inflicting wounds,\nوَ حَالُوْا بَيْنَكَ وَ بَيْنَ الرَّوَاحِ\nWA HAALU BAYNAKA WA BAYNAR RAWAAHE \nprevented you from taking any repose,\nوَ لَمْ يَبْقَ لَكَ نَاصِرٌ\nWA LAM YABQA LAKA NAASERUN \nand you had no helper remaining.\nوَ اَنْتَ مُحْتَسِبٌ صَابِرٌ\nWA ANTA MOHTASEBUN SAABERUN \nYou were bereaved yet patient, \nتَذُبُّ عَنْ نِسْوَتِكَ وَ اَوْلَادِكَ\nTAZUBBO A’N NISWATEKA WA AWLAADEKA \ndefending your women and children,\nحَتّٰى نَكَسُوْكَ عَنْ جَوَادِكَ\nHATTAA NAKASOOKA A’N JAWAADEKA \nuntil they caused you to fall from your horse.\nفَهَوَيْتَ اِلَى الْاَرْضِ جَرِيْحًا\nFAHAWAYTA ELAL ARZE JAREEHAN \nYou fell to the ground, wounded,\nتَطَؤُكَ الْخُيُوْلُ بِحَوَافِرِهَا\nTATA-OKAL KHOYOOLO BE-HAWAAFEREHAA \nhorses trampled you with their hooves,\nوَ تَعْلُوْكَ الطُّغَاةُ بِبَوَاتِرِهَا\nWA TAL-O’OKAT TOGHAATO BE-BAWAATEREHAA \ntyrants raised their swords against you,\nقَدْ رَشَحَ لِلْمَوْتِ جَبِيْنُكَ\nQAD RASHAHA LIL-MAWTE JABEENOKA \nthe sweat of death appeared on your forehead,\nوَ اخْتَلَفَتْ بِالْاِنْقِبَاضِ وَ الْاِنْبِسَاطِ شِمَالُكَ وَ يَمِيْنُكَ\nWAKH TALAFAT BIL-INQEBAAZE WAL IMBESAATE SHEMAALOKA WA YAMEENOKA \nand you continually clenched and unclenched your hands,\nتُدِيْرُ طَرْفًا خَفِيًّا اِلٰى رَحْلِكَ وَ بَيْتِكَ\nTODEERO TARFAN KHAFIYYAN ELAA RAHLEKA WA BAYTEKA \nsecretly gazing upon your caravan and tents,\nوَ قَدْ شُغِلْتَ بِنَفْسِكَ عَنْ وُلْدِكَ وَ اَهَالِيْكَ\nWA QAD SHOGHILTA BENAFSEKA A’N WULDEKA WA AHAALEEKA \nwhile trapped by yourself away from your children and family.\nوَ اَسْرَعَ فَرَسُكَ شَارِدًا اِلٰى خِيَامِكَ قاصِدًا مُحَمْحِمًا بَاكِيًا\nWA ASRA-A’ FARASOKA SHAAREDAN ELAA KHEYAAMEKA QAASEDAN MOHAMHEMAN BAAKEYAN \n(At that time,) your horse distractedly galloped towards your camp, neighing and crying.\nفَلَمَّا رَاَيْنَ النِّسَاءُ جَوَادَكَ مَخْزِيًّا\nFALLAMAA RA-AYNAN NESAA-O JAWAADAKA MAKHZIYYAN \nWhen the women saw your horse distraught, \nوَ نَظَرْنَ سَرْجَكَ عَلَيْهِ مَلْوِيًّا\nWA NAZARNA SARJAKA A’LAIHE MALWIYYAN \nand observed your saddle contorted,\nبَرَزْنَ مِنَ الْخُدُوْرِ\nBARAZNA MENAL KHODOORE \nthey came from the tents,\nنَاشِرَاتِ الشُّعُوْرِ\nNAASHERAATISH SHO-O’ORE \ndisheveling their hair,\nعَلَى الْخُدُوْدِ لَاطِمَاتِ الْوُجُوْهِ سَافِرَاتٍ\nA’LAL KHODOODE LAATEMAATIL WOJOOHE SAAFERAATIN \nstriking their now unveiled cheeks,\nوَ بِالْعَوِيْلِ دَاعِيَاتٍ\nWA BIL-A’WEELE DAAE’YAATIN \ncalling you by lamenting and wailing,\nوَ بَعْدَ الْعِزِّ مُذَلَّلَاتِ\nWA BA’DAL I’ZZE MOZALLALAATE \nbeing humiliated after being honored,\nوَ اِلٰى مَصْرَعِكَ مُبَادِرَاتٍ\nWA ELAA MASRAE’KA MOBAADERAATIN\nhastening to where you lay wounded.\nوَ الشِّمْرُ جَالِسٌ عَلٰى صَدْرِكَ\nWASH SHIMRO JAALESUN A’LAA SADREKA \nAt that time Shimr (L) was sitting on your chest,\nوَ مُوْلِغٌ سَيْفَهٗ عَلٰى نَحْرِكَ\nWA MOOLEGHUN SAIFAHU A’LAA NAHREKA \nquenching his sword with (the blood of) your throat,\nقَابِضٌ عَلٰى شَيْبَتِكَ بِيَدِهٖ\nQAABEZUN A’LAA SHAIBATEKA BEYADEHI \ngrabbing your beard with his hand,\nذَابِحٌ لَكَ بِمُهَنَّدِهٖ\nZAABEHUN LAKA BE-MOHANNADEHI \nas he slew you with his sword.\nقَدْ سَكَنَتْ حَوَاسُّكَ\nQAD SAKANAT HAWAASSOKA \nYour faculties faded,\nوَ خَفِيَتْ اَنْفَاسُكَ\nWA KHAFEYAT ANFAASOKA \nyour breath became shallow and ceased,\nوَ رُفِعَ عَلَى الْقَنَاةِ رَأْسُكَ\nWA ROFE-A’ A’LAL QANAATE RAASOKA \nand your head was raised onto a spear.\nوَ سُبِيَ اَهْلُكَ كَالْعَبِيْدِ\nWA SOBEYA AHLOKA KAL-A’BEEDE \nYour family were captured like slaves,\nوَ صُفِّدُوا فِي الْحَدِيْدِ فَوْقَ اَقْتَابِ الْمَطِيَّاتِ\nWA SUFFEDOO FIL HADEEDE FAUQA AQTAABIL MATIYYAATE \nbound with iron chains atop camels,\nتَلْفَحُ وُجُوْهَهُمْ حَرُّ الْهَاجِرَاتِ\nTALFAHO WOJOOHAHUM HARRAL HAAJERAATE \nwith midday heat scorching their faces.\nيُسَاقُوْنَ فِي الْبَرَارِيْ وَ الْفَلَوَاتِ\nYOSAAQOONA FIL BARAARI WAL FALAWAATE \nThey were driven across deserts and wastelands,\nاَيْدِيْهِمْ مَغلُوْلَةٌ اِلَى الْاَعْناقِ\nAYDEEHIM MAGHLOOLATUN ELAL AA’NAAQE \nwith their hands chained to their necks,\nيُطَافُ بِهِمْ فِي الْاَسْوَاقِ\nYOTAAFO BEHIM FIL ASWAAQE \nand were paraded around the markets.\nفَالْوَيْلُ لِلْعُصَاةِ الْفُسَّاقِ\nFALWAYLO LILO’SAATIL FUSSAAQE \nWoe be unto the wicked transgressors!\nلَقَدْ قَتَلُوْا بِقَتْلِكَ الْاِسْلَامَ\nLAQAD QATALOO BE-QATLEKAL ISLAAMA \nCertainly, by killing you, they have killed Islam,\nوَ عَطَّلُوا الصَّلٰوةَ وَ الصِّيَامَ\nWA A’TTALUS SALAATA WAS SEYAAMA \ndisrupted (the truth of) prayer and fasting, \nوَ نَقَضُوْا السُّنَنَ وَ الْاَحْكَامَ\nWA NAQAZUS SONANA WAL AHKAAMA \nrevoked the (prophetic) customs and the (divine) laws, \nوَ هَدَمُوْا قَواعِدَ الْاِيْمَانِ\nWA HADAMU QAWAAE’DAL EEMAANE \ndestroyed the pillars of faith,\nوَ حَرَّفُوْا آيَاتِ الْقُرْآنِ\nWA HARREFOO AAYAATIL QURAANE \ndistorted the verses of the Quran, \nوَ هَمْلَجُوْا فِي الْبَغْيِ وَ الْعُدْوَانِ\nWA HAMLAJOO FIL BAGYE WAL U’DWAANE \nand brutally rushed into tyranny and aggression. \nلَقَدْ اَصْبَحَ رَسُوْلُ اللهِ صَلَّى اللهُ عَلَيْهِ وَ اٰلِهٖ مَوْتُوْرًا\nLAQAD ASBAHA RASOOLUL LAAHE SALLAL LAAHO A’LAIHE WA AALEHI MAWTURAN \nCertainly, (by this event,) the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w.a.) was wronged, left alone, and denied vengeance,\nوَ عَادَ كِتَابُ اللهِ عَزَّوَجَلَّ مَهْجُوْرًا\nWA A’ADA KETABUL LAAHE A’ZZA WA JALLA MAHJOORAN \nthe Book of Allah, the mighty and the majestic, was again abandoned,\nوَ غُوْدِرَ الْحَقُّ اِذْ قُهِرْتَ مَقْهُوْرًا\nWA GOODERAL HAQQO IZ QOHERTA MAQHOORAN\ntruth was betrayed when you were forcibly overcome,\nوَ فُقِدَ بِفَقْدِكَ التَّكْبِيْرُ وَ التَّهْلِيْلُ\nWA FOQEDA BE-FAQDEKAT TAKBEERO WAT TAHLEELO \nAnd with your loss, call for Allah’s glorification and His Unity,\nوَالتَّحْرِيْمُ وَ التَّحْلِيْلُ وَ التَّنْزِيْلُ وَ التَّأْوِيْلُ\nWAT TAHREEMO WAT TAHLEELO WAT TANZEELO WAT TAAWEELO \nHis prohibitions, sanctions, revelation, and interpretation were lost.\nوَ ظَهَرَ بَعْدَكَ التَّغْيِيْرُ وَ التَّبْدِيْلُ وَ الْاِلْحَادُ وَ التَّعْطِيْلُ وَ الْاَهْوَاءُ وَ الْاَضَالِيْلُ وَ الْفِتَنُ وَ الْاَبَاطِيْلُ\nWA ZAHARA BA’DAKAT TAGYEERO WAT TABDEELO WAL ILHAADO WAT TA’TEELO WAL AHWAA-O WAL AZAALEELO WAL FETANO WAL ABAATEELO \nAfter you, alteration, distortion, infidelity, abandonment (of the Islamic laws), vagary, misguidance, turmoil and falsehood became prevalent.\nفَقَامَ نَاعِيْكَ عِنْدَ قَبْرِ جَدِّكَ الرَّسُوْلِ صَلَّى اللهُ عَلَيْهِ وَ آلِهٖ\nFAQAAMA NAAE’EKA I’NDA QABRE JADDEKAR RASOOLE SALLAL LAAHO A’LAYHE WA AALEHI \nThe announcer of your martyrdom came near the grave of your grandfather, the Messenger (s.a.w.a.),\nفَنَعَاكَ اِلَيْهِ بِالدَّمْعِ الْهَطُوْلِ قَائِلًا:\nFANA-A’AKA ELAYHE BIDDAMI’L HATOOLE QAA-ELAN: \ngave the news to him with tears flowing, saying: \nيا رَسُوْلَ اللهِ قُتِلَ سِبْطُكَ وَ فَتَاكَ\nYAA RASOOLLAL LAAHE QOTELA SIBTOKA WA FATAAKA\nO the Messenger of Allah! Your brave grandson was slain,\nوَ اسْتُبِيْحَ اَهْلُكَ وَ حِمَاكَ\nWAS TOBEEHA AHLOKA WA HEMAAKA \nand abuse of your family and supporters were deemed lawful.\nوَ سُبِيَتْ بَعْدَكَ ذَرَارِيْكَ\nWA SOBEYAT BA’DAKA ZARAAREEKA \nAfter you, your progeny were captured,\nوَ وَقَعَ الْمَحْذُوْرُ بِعِتْرَتِكَ وَ ذَوِيْكَ\nWA WAQA-A’L MAHZOORO BE-I’TRATEKA WA ZAWEEKA \nand adversity befell your family and your offspring.\nفَانْزَعَجَ الرَّسُوْلُ وَ بَكٰى قَلْبُهُ الْمَهُوْلُ\nFANZA-A’JAR RASOOLO WA BAKAA QALBOHUL MAHOOLO \nIndeed, the Messenger (s.a.w.a.) became distressed and his depressed heart wept,\nوَ عَزَّاهُ بِكَ الْمَلَائِكَةُ وَ الْاَنْبِيَاءُ\nWA A’ZZAAHO BEKAL MALAAAEKATO WAL AMBEYAA-O \nThe Angels and the prophets offered their condolences to him for your martyrdom, \nوَ فُجِعَتْ بِكَ اُمُّكَ الزَّهْرَاءُ\nWA FOJEA’T BEKA UMMOKAZ ZAHRAAO \nYour mother, al-Zahra, became distressed and bereft of you, \nوَ اخْتَلَفَتْ جُنُوْدُ الْمَلَائِكَةِ الْمُقَرَّبِيْنَ تُعَزّٰي اَبَاكَ اَمِيْرَالْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ\nWAKH TALAFAT JONOODUL MALAAAEKATIL MOQARRABEENA TOA’ZZAA ABAAKA AMEERAL MOAMENEENA \nLegions of favored Angels came in waves to offer their condolences to your father, the Leader of the Faithful,\nوَ اُقِيْمَتْ لَكَ الْمَآتِمُ فِيْ اَعْلَا عِلِّيّيْنَ\nWA OQEEMAT LAKAL MAAATEMO FI AA’LAA I’LLIYYEENA \nMourning commemorations were held for you in the utmost exalted place Heaven,\nوَ لَطَمَتْ عَلَيْكَ الْحُوْرُ الْعِيْنُ\nWA LOTEMAT A’LAIKAL HOORUL E’ENO \nand the dark-eyed Maidens (of Paradise) hit their own heads and faces in grief, \nوَ بَكَتِ السَّمَاءُ وَ سُكَّانُهَا\nWA BAKATIS SAMAAO WA SUKKAANOHA \nThe skies and their inhabitants wept,\nوَ الْجِنَانُ وَ خُزَّانُهَا\nWAL JENAANO WA KHUZZAANOHA \nas did Paradise and its keepers,\nوَ الْهِضَابُ وَ اَقْطَارُهَا\nWAL HEZAABO WA AQTAAROHA \nthe mountains and their surroundings,\nوَ الْبِحَارُ وَ حِيْتَانُهَا\nWAL BEHAARO WA HEETAANOHA \nthe oceans and their fishes,\nوَ الْجِنَانُ وَ وِلْدَانُهَا\nWAL JENAANO WA WILDAANOHA \nthe heavens and their servants,\nوَ الْبَيْتُ وَ الْمَقَامُ\nWAL BAYTO WAL MAQAAMO \nthe House (Ka’ba), and the Station (of Abraham),\nوَ الْمَشْعَرُ الْحَرَامُ\nWAL MASH-A’RUL HARAAMO \nthe Sacred Monument,\nوَ الْحِلُّ وَ الْاِحْرَامُ\nWAL HILLO WAL EHRAAMO\nand Mecca and its sanctuary.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ فَبِحُرْمَةِ هٰذَا الْمَكَانِ الْمُنِيْفِ\nALLAAHUMMA FABEHURMATIL MAKAANIL MONEEFE \nO Allah! By the sanctity of this exalted place (the tomb of Imam al-Husain (a.s.)),\nصَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَ آلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nSALLE A’LAA MOHAMMADIN WA AALE MOHAMMADIN \nbestow blessings upon Muhammad and the family of Muhammad,\nوَاحْشُرْنِيْ فِيْ زُمْرَتِهِمْ\nWAH SHURNEE FEE ZUMRATEHIM \nassemble me in their company,\nوَ اَدْخِلْنِي الْجَنَّةَ بِشَفَاعَتِهِمْ\nWA ADKHILNIL JANNATA BE-SHAFAA-A’TEHIM \nand admit me to Paradise by their intercession.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنّي اَتَوَسَّلُ اِلَيْكَ يا اَسْرَعَ الْحَاسِبِيْنَ\nALLAHUMMA INNEE ATAWASSALO E’LAYKA YAA ASRA-A’L HAASEBEENA \nMy Allah! I implore You, O He who is the quickest of the reckoners!\nوَ يَااَكْرَمَ الْاَكْرَمِيْنَ وَ يَااَحْكَمَ الْحَاكِمِيْنَ\nWA YAA AKRAMAL AKRAMEENA WA YAA AHKAMA-L HAAKEMEENA \nO the most generous of the generous and the wisest of judges!\nبِمُحَمَّدٍ خَاتَمِ النَّبِيِّيْنَ رَسُوْلِكَ اِلَى الْعَالَمِيْنَ اَجْمَعِيْنَ\nBE-MOHAMMADIN KHAATAMIN NABIYYEENA RASOOLEKA ELAL A’ALAMEENA AJMAE’EN \nBy Muhammad, the seal of the prophets, Your Messenger to all the worlds,\nوَ بِاَخِيْهِ وَ ابْنِ عَمِّهِ الْاَنْزَعِ الْبَطِيْنِ الْعَالِمِ الْمَكِيْنِ عَلِيٍّ اَمِيْرِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ\nWA BE-AKHEEHE WAB NA A’MMEHIL ANZAI’L BATEENIL A’ALEMIL MAKEENE A’LIYYIN AMEERIL MOMENEENA \nBy his brother and cousin, the uprooter of hidden polytheism, the distinguished and learned, Ali, the Prince of the Faithful,\nوَ بِفَاطِمَةَ سَيِّدَةِ نِسَاءِ الْعَالَمِيْنَ\nWA BE-FAATEMATA SAYYEDATE NESAAIL A’ALAMEENA \nBy Fatima, the chief of women of the worlds,\nوَ بِالْحَسَنِ الزَّكِيِّ عِصْمَةِ الْمُتَّقِيْنَ\nWA BIL HASANIZ ZAKIYYE I’SMATIL MUTTAQEENA \nBy al-Hasan, the purified one and the protection of the pious,\nوَ بِاَبِيْ عَبْدِاللهِ الْحُسَيْنِ اَكْرَمِ الْمُسْتَشْهَدِيْنَ\nWA BE-ABI A’BDIL LAAHIL HUSAYNE AKRAMIL MUSTASHHADEENA \nBy Abi Abdillah, al-Husain, the most honored martyr,\nوَ بِاَوْلَادِهِ الْمَقْتُوْلِيْنَ وَ بِعِتْرَتِهِ الْمَظْلُوْمِيْنَ\nWA BE-AWLAADEHIL MAQTOOLEENA WA BE-I’TRATEHIL MAZLOOMEENA \nBy his slain children and oppressed family,\nوَ بِعَلِيِّ بْنِ الْحُسَيْنِ زَيْنِ الْعَابِدِيْنَ\nWA BE-A’LI YIBNIL HUSAYNE ZAINIL A’ABEDEENA\nBy Ali Ibn al-Husain, the ornament of the worshippers,\nوَ بِمُحَمَّدِ بْنِ عَلِيٍّ قِبْلَةِ الْاَوَّابِيْنَ\nWA MOHAMMAD IBNE A’LIYYIN QIBLATIL AWWAABEENA \nBy Muhammad Ibn Ali, the direction of those who turn to Allah,\nوَ جَعْفَرِ بْنِ مُحَمَّدٍ اَصْدَقِ الصَّادِقِيْنَ\nWA JA’FAR IBNE MOHAMMADIN ASDAQIS SAADEQEENA \nBy Ja’far Ibn Muhammad, the most truthful,\nوَ مُوسٰى بْنِ جَعْفَرٍ مُظْهِرِ الْبَرَاهِيْنَ\nWA MUSA IBNE JA’FARIN MUZHERIL BARAAHEENA \nBy Musa Ibn Ja’far, the discloser of the proofs,\nوَ عَلِيِّ بْنِ مُوْسٰى نَاصِرِ الدِّيْنِ\nWA A’LIYYIBNE MOOSA NAASERID DEENE \nBy Ali Ibn Musa, the helper of the religion,\nوَ مُحَمَّدِ بْنِ عَلِيٍّ قُدْوَةِ الْمُهْتَدِيْنَ\nWA MOHAMMAD IBNE A’LIYYIN QUDWATIL MOHTADEENA \nBy Muhammad Ibn Ali, the exemplar of those who accepted guidance,\nوَ عَلِيِّ بْنِ مُحَمَّدٍ اَزْهَدِ الزّاهِدِيْنَ\nWA A’LIYYIBNE MOHAMMADIN AZHADIZ ZAAHEDEENA \nBy Ali Ibn Muhammad, the most ascetic,\nوَ الْحَسَنِ بْنِ عَلِيٍّ وارِثِ الْمُسْتَخْلَفِيْنَ\nWAL HASAN IBNE A’LIYYIN WAARESIL MUSTAKHLAFEENA \nBy Hasan Ibn Ali, the inheritor of the appointed ones,\nوَالْحُجَّةِ عَلَى الْخَلْقِ اَجْمَعِيْنَ\nWAL HUJJATE A’LAL KHALQE AJMAE’ENA \nBy the Proof upon all creation (al-Mahdi),\nاَنْ تُصَلِّيَ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَ آلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nAN TOSALLEYA A’LAA MOHAMMADIN WA AALE MOHAMMADENIS \nBless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad,\nالصَّادِقِيْنَ الْاَبَرِّيْنَ آلِ طٰهٰ وَ يٰسٓ\nSAADEQEENAL ABARREENA AALE TAAHAA WA YAASIN \nthe most truthful and devoted ones (who are) the family of Taha and Yasin,\nوَ اَنْ تَجْعَلَنِيْ فِي الْقِيَامَةِ مِنَ الْآمِنِيْنَ الْمُطْمَئِنِّيْنَ\nWA AN TAJ-A’LANI FIL QEYAAMATE MENAL AAMENEENAL MUTMAINNEENAL \nand place me on the Day of Judgment among those who are safe, confident, \nالْفَائِزِيْنَ الْفَرِحِيْنَ الْمُسْتَبْشِرِيْنَ\nFAAEZEENAL FAREHEENAL MUSTABSHEREENA \ntriumphant, happy, and felicitous.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اكْتُبْنِيْ فِي الْمُسْلِمِيْنَ\nALLAAHUMMAK TUBNEE FIL MUSLEMEENA\nO Allah! Destine me to be amongst the submitters,\nوَ اَلْحِقْنِي بِالصَّالِحِيْنَ\nWA ALHIQNEE BIS-SAALEHEENA \nJoin me with the righteous,\nوَاجْعَلْ لِيْ لِسَانَ صِدْقٍ فِي الْآخِرِيْنَ\nWAJ A’L LEE LESAANA SIDQIN FIL AAKHEREENA \nOrdain for me (offspring with) truthful tongue among the last generation,\nوَانْصُرْنِيْ عَلَى الْبَاغِيْنَ\nWAN SURNEE A’LAL BAAGHEENA \nMake me victorious over the transgressors,\nوَاكْفِنِيْ كَيْدَ الْحَاسِدِيْنَ\nWAK FENEE KAYDAL HAASEDEENA \nSuffice me the deception of the envious, \nوَاصْرِفْ عَنِّي مَكْرَ الْمَاكِرِيْنَ\nWAS RIF A’NNEE MAKRAL MAAKEREENA \nTurn away from me the evil plans of the schemers,\nوَاقْبِضْ عَنِّي اَيْدِيَ الظَّالِمِيْنَ\nWAQ BIZ A’NNEE AYDIZ ZAALEMEENA \nHold back from me the hands of the oppressors,\nوَاجْمَعْ بَيْنِيْ وَ بَيْنَ السَّادَةِ الْمَيَامِيْنِ فِيْ اَعْلَا عِلِّيِّيْنَ\nWAJ MA’ BAYNEE WA BAYNAS SAADATIL MAYAAMEENA FEE AA’LAA I’LLIYYEENA \nGather me with the blessed masters in the utmost exalted place of Heaven,\nمَعَ الَّذِيْنَ اَنْعَمْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ مِنَ النَّبِيِّيْنَ وَ الصِّدِّيْقِيْنَ وَ الشُّهَدَاءِ وَ الصَّالِحِيْنَ\nMA’AL LAZEENA AN-A’MTA A’LAYHIM MENAN NABIYYEENA WAS SIDDEEQEENA WASH SHOHADAAE WAS SAALEHEENA \nalong with whom You have bestowed favor, from among the prophets, the truthful, the martyrs, and the righteous,\nبِرَحْمَتِكَ يا اَرْحَمَ الرّاحِمِيْنَ\nBE-RAHMATEKA YAA ARHAMAR RAAHEMEENA\nBy Your mercy, O the most merciful of the merciful.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنّي اُقْسِمُ عَلَيْكَ بِنَبِيِّكَ الْمَعْصُوْمِ\nALLAAHUMMA INNI UQSEMO A’LAYKA BE-NABIYYEKAL MA’SOOME \nO Allah! I implore You by Your infallible Prophet,\nوَ بِحُكْمِكَ الْمَحْتُومِ وَ نُهْيَكَ [نَهْيِكَ] الْمَكْتُوْمِ\nWA BE-HUKMEKAL MAHTOOME WA NOHYAKA (NAHYEKAL) MAKTOOME \nby Your definite judgment, and Your concealed preventive wisdom,\nوَ بِهٰذَا الْقَبْرِ الْمَلْمُوْمِ الْمُوَسَّدِ فِيْ كَنَفِهِ الْاِمَامُ الْمَعْصُوْمُ الْمَقْتُوْلُ الْمَظْلُوْمُ\nWA BEHAAZAL QABRIL MALMOOMIL MOWASSADE FI KANAFEHIL EMAAMUL MA’SOOMUL MAQTOOLUL MAZLOOMO \nby this grave which is the place of congregation and in which lies the infallible Imam, the slaughtered, and the oppressed,\nاَنْ تَكْشِفَ مَا بِيْ مِنَ الْغُمُوْمِ\nAN TAKSHEFA MAA BEE MENAL GHOMOOME \nthat You dispel from me all that grieves me,\nوَ تَصْرِفَ عَنّٰي شَرَّ الْقَدَرِ الْمَحْتُوْمِ\nWA TASREFA A’NNAA SHARRAL QADARIL MAHTOOME \ndivert from me the harm of the decisive foreordained plan,\nوَ تُجِيْرَنِيْ مِنَ النَّارِ ذَاتِ السَّمُوْمِ\nWA TOJEERANI MENAN NAARE ZAATIS SAMOOME \nand give me refuge from the Hellfire with scorching winds.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ جَلِّلْنِيْ بِنِعْمَتِكَ\nALLAAHUMMA JALLILNEE BE-NE’MATEKA \nMy Allah! Honor me with Your bounties,\nوَ رَضِّنِيْ بِقَسْمِكَ\nWA RAZZENEE BE-QASMEKA \nMake me content with Your apportionment,\nوَ تَغَمَّدْنِيْ بِجُوْدِكَ وَ كَرَمِكَ\nWA TAGAMMADNEE BE-JOODEKA WA KARAMEKA \nEncompass me with Your munificence and generosity,\nوَ بَاعِدْنِيْ مِنْ مَكْرِكَ وَ نِقْمَتِكَ\nWA BAA-I’DNEE MIN MAKREKA WA NIQMATEKA \nAnd keep me far off from Your requital scheme and Your wrath. \nاَللّٰهُمَّ اعْصِمْنِيْ مِنَ الزَّلَلِ\nALLAAHUMMA’ SIMNEE MENAZ ZALALE \nO Allah! Protect me from errors,\nوَ سَدِّدْنِيْ فِي الْقَوْلِ وَ الْعَمَلِ\nWA SADDIDNEE FIL QAWLE WAL A’MALE \nMake me firm in speech and action,\nوَافْسَحْ لِيْ فِيْ مُدَّةِ الْاَجَلِ\nWAF SAH LEE FEE MUDDATIL AJALE \nExtend for me the period (of life), \nوَ اعْفِنِيْ مِنَ الْاَوْجَاعِ وَ الْعِلَلِ\nWA’ FENEE MENAL AWJAAE’ WAL E’LALE\nRelieve me from pain and ailments, \nوَ بَلِّغْنِيْ بِمَوَالِيَّ وَ بِفَضْلِكَ اَفْضَلَ الْاَمَلِ\nWA BALLIGNI BE-MAWAALIYYA WA BE-FAZLEKA AFZALAL AMALE\nMake me achieve, through my masters and Your grace, the best of wishes.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَ آلِ مُحَمَّدٍ وَ اقْبَلْ تَوْبَتِيْ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLE A’LAA MOHAMMADIN WA AALE MOHAMMADIN WAQ BAL TAWBATEE \nO Allah! Bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad and accept my repentance and my return,\nوَارْحَمْ عَبْرَتِيْ\nWAR HAM A’BRATEE\nHave mercy upon my weeping,\nوَ اَقِلْنِيْ عَثْرَتِيْ\nWA AQILNEE A’SRATEE \nLessen my lapses,\nوَ نَفِّسْ كُرْبَتِيْ\nWA NAFFIS KURBATEE\nRelieve my distress,\nوَاغْفِرْ لِيْ خَطِيْئَتِيْ\nWAGH FIR LEE KHATEEATEE \nForgive me my mistake, \nوَ اَصْلِحْ لِيْ فِيْ ذُرِّيَّتِيْ\nWA ASLEH LEE FEE ZURRIYYATEE \nAnd improve my (righteousness) through my children.\nاَللّغٰهُمَّ لَا تَدَعْ لِيْ فِيْ هٰذَا الْمَشْهَدِ الْمُعَظَّمِ وَ الْمَحَلِّ الْمُكَرَّمِ ذَنْبًااِلاَّ غَفَرْتَهٗ\nALLAAHUMMA LAA TADA’LEE FEE HAAZAL MASH-HADIL MOA’ZZAME WAL MAHALLIL MOKARRAME ZAMBAN ILLAA GAFARTAHU \nMy Allah! Do not leave for me, in this exalted and honored place of martyrdom, any sin but that You forgive,\nوَ لَا عَيْبًا اِلاَّ سَتَرْتَهٗ\nWA LAA A’YBAN ILLAA SATARTAHU \nNor any defect but that You conceal,\nوَ لَا غَمًّا اِلاَّ كَشَفْتَهٗ\nWA LAA GHAMMAN ILLAA KASHAFTAHU \nNor any grief but that You remove,\nوَ لَا رِزْقًا اِلَّا بَسَطْتَهٗ\nWA LAA RIZQAN ILLAA BASATTAHU \nNor any sustenance but that You extend,\nوَ لَا جَاهًا اِلَّا عَمَرْتَهٗ\nWA LAA JAAHAN ILLAA A’MARTAHU \nNor any (spiritual) status but that You cause to prosper,\nوَ لَا فَسَادًا اِلَّا اَصْلَحْتَهٗ\nWA LAA FASAADAN ILLAA ASLAHTAHU \nNor any corruption but that which You correct,\nوَ لَا اَمَلًا اِلَّا بَلَّغْتَهٗ\nWA LAA AMALAN ILLAA BALLAGTAHU \nNor any wish but that You fulfill,\nوَ لَا دُعَاءً اِلَّا اَجَبْتَهٗ\nWA LAA DOA’A-AN ILLAA AJABTAHU \nNor any supplication but that You answer,\nوَ لَا مَضِيْقًا اِلَّا فَرَّجْتَهٗ\nWA LAA MAZEEQAN ILLAA FARRAJTAHU \nNor any pressure but that You relieve,\nوَ لَا شَمْلًا اِلَّا جَمَعْتَهٗ\nWA LAA SHAMLAN ILLAA JAMA’TAHU\nNor any dispersed (believers) but that You reunify,\nوَ لَا اَمْرًا اِلَّا اَتْمَمْتَهٗ\nWA LAA AMRAN ILLAA ATMAMTAHU \nNor any matter but that You complete,\nوَ لَا مَالًا اِلَّا كَثَّرْتَهٗ\nWA LAA MAALAN ILLAA KASSARTAHU \nNor any wealth but that You increase,\nوَ لَا خُلْقًا اِلَّا حَسَّنْتَهٗ\nWA LAA KHULQAN ILLAA HASSANTAHU \nNor any character but that You improve,\nوَ لَا اِنْفَاقًا اِلَّا اَخْلَفْتَهٗ\nWA LAA INFAAQAN ILLAA AKHLAFTAHU \nNor any charity but that You repay,\nوَ لَا حَالًا اِلَّا عَمَرْتَهٗ\nWA LAA HAALAN ILLAA A’MARTAHU \nNor any condition but that You cause to improve, \nوَ لَا حَسُوْدًا اِلَّا قَمَعْتَهٗ\nWA LAA HASOODAN ILLAA QAMA’TAHU \nNor any envious (one) but that You suppress,\nوَ لَا عَدُوًّا اِلَّا اَرْدَيْتَهٗ\nWA LAA A’DUWWAN ILLAA ARDAYTAHU \nNor any enemy but that You destroy,\nوَ لَا شَرًّا اِلَّا كَفَيْتَهٗ\nWA LAA SHARRAN ILLAA KAFAYTAHU \nNor any evil but that You suffice,\nوَ لَا مَرَضًا اِلَّا شَفَيْتَهٗ\nWA LAA MARZAN ILLAA SHAFAYTAHU \nNor any ailment but that You cure,\nوَ لَا بَعِيْدًا اِلَّا اَدْنَيْتَهٗ\nWA LAA BAE’EDAN ILLAA ADNAYTAHU \nNor any distant (one) but that You bring near,\nوَ لَا شَعِثًا اِلَّا لَمَمْتَهٗ\nWA LAA SHA’SAN ILLAA LAMAMTAHU \nNor any scattering but that You reunite,\nوَ لَا سُؤَالًا [سُؤْلًا] اِلَّا اَعْطَيْتَهٗ\nWA LAA SOAALAN (SOALAN) ILLAA A’ATAYTAHU\nNor any request but that You grant.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنّيِ اَسْئَلُكَ خَيْرَ الْعَاجِلَةِ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE ASALOKA KHAYRAL A’AJELATE \nO Allah! I ask You for the goodness of this transitory world,\nوَ ثَوَابَ الْآجِلَةِ\nWA SAWAABAL AAJELATE \nand the reward of the hereafter.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اَغْنِنِيْ بِحَلَالِكَ عَنِ الْحَرَامِ\nALLAAHUMMA AGNENEE BE-HALAALEKA A’NIL HARAAME \nO Allah! Suffice me with what You made lawful from the unlawful,\nوَ بِفَضْلِكَ عَنْ جَمِيْعِ الْاَنَامِ\nWA BE-FAZLEKA A’N JAMEEI’L ANAAME \nand with Your grace from all other creatures.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنّيِ اَسْئَلُكَ عِلْمًا نَافِعًا\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE ASALOKA I’LMAN NAAFEA’N \nMy Allah! I ask You for beneficial knowledge,\nوَ قَلْبًا خَاشِعًا\nWA QALBAN KHAASHEAN \na humble heart, \nوَ يَقِيْنًا شَافِيًا\nWA YAQEENAN SHAAFEYAN \nunequivocal certitude, \nوَ عَمَلًا زَاكِيًا\nWA A’MALAN ZAAKEYAN \npure action, \nوَ صَبْرًا جَمِيْلًا\nWA SABRAN JAMEELAN \nbeautiful patience,\nوَ اَجْرًا جَزِيْلًا\nWA AJRAN JAZEELAN\nand a bountiful reward. \nاَللّٰهُمَّ ارْزُقْنِيْ شُكْرَ نِعْمَتِكَ عَلَىَّ\nALLAAHUMMAR ZUQNEE SHUKRA NE’MATEKA A’LAYYA \nO Allah! Grant me gratitude of Your blessing upon me,\nوَ زِدْ فِيْ اِحْسَانِكَ وَ كَرَمِكَ اِلَىَّ\nWA ZID FEE EHSAANEKA WA KARAMEKA ELAYYA \nIncrease Your favor and munificence on me,\nوَ اجْعَلْ قَوْلِيْ فِي النَّاسِ مَسْمُوْعًا\nWAJ A’L QAWLEE FINNAASE MASMOOA’N \nMake my speech amongst people effective,\nوَ عَمَلِيْ عِنْدَكَ مَرْفُوْعًا\nWA A’MALEE I’NDAKA MARFOOA’N \nmy deeds elevated and worthy of being delivered to You,\nوَ اَثَرِيْ فِي الْخَيْرَاتِ مَتْبُوْعًا\nWA ASAREE FIL KHAYRAATE MATBOOA’N \nmy righteous works followed (by others),\nوَ عَدُوِّيْ مَقْمُوْعًا\nWA A’DUWWEE MAQMOOA’N\nand my enemy quelled,\nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَ آلِ مُحَمَّدٍ الْاَخْيَارِ فِيْ آنَاءِ اللَّيْلِ وَ اَطْرَافِ النَّهَارِ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLE A’LAA MOHAMMADIN WA AALE MOHAMMADENIL AKHYAARE FEE AANAAIL LAYLE WA ATRAAFIN NAHAARE \nO Allah! Send blessings upon Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, the best of the creations, day and night,\nوَ اكْفِنِيْ شَرَّ الْاَشْرَارِ\nWAK FENI SHARRAL ASHRAARE \nSpare me from the evil of the wicked, \nوَ طَهِرْنِيْ مِنَ الذُّنُوْبِ وَ الْاَوْزَارِ\nWA TAHHIRNEE MENAZ ZONOOBE WAL AWZAARE \nPurify me from sins and burdens,\nوَ اَجِرْنِيْ مِنَ النَّارِ\nWA AJIRNEE MENAN NAARE \nGive me refuge from Hell-fire,\nوَ اَحِلَّنِيْ دَارَالْقَرَارِ\nWA AHILLANI DAARAL QARAARE \nSettle me in the House of rest (Paradise),\nوَ اغْفِرْ لِيْ وَ لِجَمِيْعِ اِخْوَانِيْ فِيْكَ وَ اَخَوَاتِيَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ وَ الْمُؤْمِنَاتِ\nWAGH FIR LEE WA LE-JAMEE-E’ IKHWAANEE FEEKA WA AKHAWAATEYAL MOAMENEENA WAL MOAMENAATE \nAnd forgive me and all my faithful brothers and sisters,\nبِرَحْمَتِكَ يَا اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِيْنَ.\nBE-RAHMATEKA YAA ARHAMAR RAAHEMEENA.",
