    "Supplication in the Qunut of the Prayer after Ziyarat\nThen stand beside the upper side of the grave, face towards the Qibla and perform a two-unit Ziyarat prayer. Recite Chapter 21 (al-Anbiya) in the first unit and Chapter 59 (al-Hashr) in the second unit of the prayer, and recite the following supplication in the Qunut of the prayer:\nلَااِلٰهَ اِلاَّ اللهُ الْحَلِيْمُ الْكَرِيْمُ\nLAA ELAAHA ILLAL LAAHUL HALEEMUL KAREEMO\nThere is no deity but Allah, the forbearing, the generous.\nلَا اِلٰهَ اِلاَّاللهُ الْعَلِيُّ الْعَظِيْمُ\nLAA ELAAHA ILLAL LAAHUL A’LIYYUL A’ZEEMO\nThere is no deity but Allah, the supreme, the great.\nلَا اِلٰهَ اِلاَّاللهُ رَبُّ السَّمَاوَاتِ السَّبْعِ وَ الْاَرَضِيْنَ السَّبْعِ\nLAA ELAAHA ILLAL LAAHO RABBUS SAMAAWAATIS SAB-E’ WAL ARAZEENAS SAB-E’\nThere is no deity but Allah, the Lord of the seven heavens and the seven earths,\nوَ مَا فِيْهِنَّ وَ ما بَيْنَهُنَّ\nWA MAA FEEHINNA WA MAA BAYNAHUNNA\nand whatever is in them and whatever is between them.\nخِلَافًا لِاَعْدَائِهٖ\nKHELAAFAN LE-A-A’DAA-EHI\n(By this, I am) opposing (the belief of) His enemies,\nوَ تَكْذِيْبًا لِمَنْ عَدَلَ بِهٖ\nWA TAKZEEBAN LEMAN A’DALA BEHI\ndisavowing whomever has turned away from Him,\nوَ اِقْرَارًا لِرُبُوبِيَّتِهٖ\nWA IQRAARAN LE-ROBOOBIYYATEHI\nconfessing His Lordship,\nوَ خُضُوْعًا لِعِزَّتِهِ\nWA KHOZOO-A’N LE-I’ZZATEHIL\nand surrendering to His majesty.\nالْاَوَّلُ بِغَيْرِ اَوَّلٍ\nAWWALO BE-GHAYRE AWWALIN\nHe is the first other than being the first (in number).\nوَالْآخِرُ اِلٰى غَيْرِ آخِرٍ\nWAL AAKHERO ELAA GHAYRE AAKHERENIZ\nHe is the last without having an end.\nالظَّاهِرُ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ بِقُدْرَتِهِ\nZAAHERO A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN BE-QUDRATEHIL\nHe is dominant (Zahir) over everything by His power.\nالْبَاطِنُ دُوْنَ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ بِعِلْمِهٖ وَ لُطْفِهٖ\nBAATENO DOONA KULLE SHAY-IN BE-I’LMEHI WA LUTFEHI\nHe is hidden (Batin) as He knows underneath of every thing by His knowledge and His subtlety.\nلَا تَقِفُ الْعُقُوْلُ عَلٰى كُنْهِ عَظَمَتِهٖ\nLAA TAQEFUL O’QOOLO A’LAA KUNHE A’ZAMATEHI\nIntellects cannot comprehend the depth of His grandeur.\nوَ لَا تُدْرِكُ الْاَوْهَامُ حَقِيْقَةَ مَاهِيَّتِهٖ\nWA LAA TUDREKUL AWHAAMO HAQEETATA MAAHIYYATEHI\nThoughts cannot grasp the reality of His Essence.\nوَ لَا تَتَصَوَّرُ الْاَنْفُسُ مَعَانِيَ كَيْفِيَّتِهٖ\nWA LAA TATASAWWARUL ANFOSO MA-A’ANEYA KAYFIYYATEHI\nSouls cannot imagine the meanings of His (created) qualities.\nمُطَّلِعًا عَلَى الضَّمَائِرِ\nMUTTALE-A’N A’LAZ ZAMAA-ERE\nHe knows well the innermost thoughts (of His servants),\nعَارِفًا بِالسَّرَائِرِ\nA’AREFAN BIS-SARAA-ERE\nis cognizant of the secrets,\nيَعْلَمُ خائِنَةَ الْاَعْيُنِ وَ مَا تُخْفِى الصُّدُوْرُ\nYA’LAMO KHAAENATAL A-A’YONE WA MAA TUKHFIS SODOORO\nand knows the treachery of the eyes, and all that the hearts (of men) conceal.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّي اُشْهِدُكَ عَلٰى تَصْدِيْقِيْ رَسُولَكَ صَلَّى اللهُ عَلَيْهِ وَ آلِهٖ وَ اِيْمَانِيْ بِهٖ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE USH-HEDOKA A’LAA TASDEEQEE RASOOLAKA SALLAL LAAHO A’LAYHE WA AALEHI WA EEMAANEE BEHI\nMy Allah! I bear You as witness of my acknowledgement of Your Messenger (s.a.w.a.) and my faith in him,\nوَ عِلْمِيْ بِمَنْزِلَتِهٖ\nWA I’LMEE BE-MANZELATEHI\nand my recognition of his status.\nوَ اِنِّي اَشْهَدُ اَنَّهُ النَّبِيُّ الَّذِيْ نَطَقَتِ الْحِكْمَةُ بِفَضْلِهٖ\nWA INNEE ASH-HADO ANNAHUN NABIYYUL LAZEE NATAQATIL HIKMATO BE-FAZLEHI\nI bear witness that he was the Prophet by whose favor wisdom was given voice,\nوَ بَشَّرَتِ الْاَنْبِيَاءُ بِهٖ\nWA BASHSHARTIL ANBEYAAO BEHI\nof whom (previous) prophets gave glad tidings,\nوَ دَعَتْ اِلَى الْاِقْرَارِ بِمَا جَاءَ بِهٖ\nWA DA-A’T ELAL IQRAARE BEMAA JAA-A BEHI\ncalled people to admit what he  brought (from the Lord),\nوَ حَثَّتْ عَلٰى تَصْدِيْقِهٖ\nWA HASSAT A’LAA TASDEEQEHI\nand urged people to acknowledge him,\nبِقَوْلِهٖ تَعَالٰى: «اَلَّذي يَجِدُوْنَهٗ مَكْتُوْبًا عِنْدَهُمْ فِي التَّوْرٰيةِ وَ الْاِنْجِيْلِ يَأْمُرُهُمْ بِالْمَعْرُوْفِ وَ يَنْهٰيهُمْ عَنِ الْمُنْكَرِ وَ يُحِلُّ لَهُمُ الطَّيِّبَاتِ وَ يُحَرِّمُ عَلَيْهِمُ الْخَبَائِثَ وَ يَضَعُ عَنْهُمْ اِصْرَهُمْ وَ الْاَغْلَالَ الَّتِيْ كَانَتْ عَلَيْهِمْ»\nBE-QAWLEHI TA-A’ALAA: “ALLAZEE YAJEDOONAHU MAKTOOBAN I’NDAHUM FIT TAWRAATE WAL INJEELE YAAMOROHUM BIL-MA’ROOFE WA YANHAAHUM A’NIL MUNKARE WA YOHILLO LAHOMUT TAYYEBAATE WA YOHARREMO A’LAYHEMUL KHABAA-ESA WA YA-ZA-O’ A’NHUM ISRAHUM WAL AGHLAALAL LATEE KAANAT A’LAYHIM.”\naccording to His saying, the most high, “… he, whom they find mentioned in their Torah and the Gospels, who commands them virtuous acts and forbids them evil, allows them as lawful the good (and pure) things, prohibits them from impurities, and releases them from their heavy burdens and from the yokes that are upon them ...”\nفَصَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ رَسُوْلِكَ اِلَى الثَّقَلَيْنِ\nFA-SALLE A’LAA MOHAMMADIN RASOOLEKA ELAS SAQALAYNE\nThus, bless Muhammad, Your messenger to both masses (of human and Jinn),\nوَ سَيِّدِ الْاَنْبِيَاءِ الْمُصْطَفَيْنَ\nWA SAYYEDIL AMBIYAA-IL MUSTAFAYNA\nthe master of the chosen prophets,\nوَ عَلٰى اَخِيْهِ وَ ابْنِ عَمِّهٖ\nWA A’LAA AKHEEHE WAB NE A’MMEHIL\nand (bless) his brother and his cousin,\nاللَّذَيْنِ لَمْ يُشْرِكَا بِكَ طَرْفَةَ عَيْنٍ اَبَدًا\nLAZAYNE LAM YUSHREKAA BEKA TARFATA A’YNIN ABADAN\nneither of whom ever took associates with You (in worship) even for one moment,\nوَ عَلٰى فاطِمَةَ الزَّهْرَاءِ سَيِّدَةِ نِسَاءِ الْعَالَمِيْنَ\nWA A’LAA FAATEMATAZ ZAHRAA-E SAYYEDATE NESAA-IL A’ALAMEENA\nand (bless) Fatima, the radiant, and the chief of the ladies of the worlds,\nوَ عَلٰى سَيِّدَىْ شَبَابِ اَهْلِ الْجَنَّةِ الْحَسَنِ وَ الْحُسَيْنِ\nWA A’LAA SAYYEDAY SHABAABE AHLIL JANNATIL HASANE WAL HUSAYNE\nand (bless) the two masters of the youth of Paradise, al-Hasan and al-Husain,\nصَلَاةً خَالِدَةَ الدَّوَامِ\nSALAATAN KHAALEDATAD DAWAAME\nWith an everlasting blessing,\nعَدَدَ قَطْرِ الرِّهَامِ\nA’DADA QATRIR REHAAME\nequal to the number of drops of rains,\nوَ زِنَةَ الْجِبَالِ وَ الْآكَامِ\nWA ZENATAL JEBAALE WAL AAKAAME\nand the weight of the mountains and hills,\nمَا اَوْرَقَ السَّلَامُ\nMAA AWRAQAS SALAAMO\nuntil peace and salutations is ever exchanged,\nوَ اخْتَلَفَ الضِّيَاءُ وَ الظَّلَامُ\nWAKH TALAFAZ ZEYAA-O WAZ ZALAAMO\nand brightness (of day) and darkness (of night) are replaced. \nوَ عَلٰى آلِهِ الطَّاهِرِيْنَ الْاَئِمَّةِ الْمُهْتَدِيْنَ\nWA A’LAA AALEHIT TAAHERENAL A-IMMATIL MOHTADEENAZ\nAnd (bless) his pure family, (the rest of) the guided Imams,\nالذَّائِدِيْنَ عَنِ الدِّيْنِ\nZAA-EDEENA A’NID DEENE\nthe defenders of the religion,\nعَلِيٍّ وَ مُحَمَّدٍ وَ جَعْفَرٍ وَ مُوْسٰى وَ عَلِيٍّ وَ مُحَمَّدٍ وَ عَلِيٍّ وَ الْحَسَنِ وَ الْحُجَّةِ\nA’LIYYIN WA MOHAMMADIN WA JA’FARIN WA MOOSAA WA A’LIYYIN WA MOHAMMADIN WA A’LIYYIN WAL HASANE WAL HUJJATIL\n(who are) Ali, Muhammad, Ja’far, Musa, Ali, Muhammad, Ali, al-Hasan, and al-Hujja,\nالْقَوَّامِ بِالْقِسْطِ وَ سُلَالَةِ السِّبْطِ\nQAWWAAME BIL-QISTE WA SOAALATIS SIBTE\nthe establishers of fairness, and the grandsons of the Prophet (s.a.w.a.).\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّي اَسْئَلُكَ بِحَقِّ هٰذَا الْاِمَامِ فَرَجًا قَرِيْبًا\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS-ALOKA BEHAQQE HAAZAL EMAAME FARAJAN QAREEBAN\nO Allah! I ask You by the rights of this Imam, a relief in the near future,\nوَ صَبْرًا جَمِيْلًا\nWA SABRAN JAMEELAN\nbeautiful patience,\nوَ نَصْرًا عَزِيْزًا\nWA NASRAN A’ZEEZAN\nmighty triumph,\nوَ غِنًى عَنِ الْخَلْقِ\nWA GHENAN A’NIL KHALQE\nsufficiency from people,\nوَ ثَبَاتًا فِي الْهُدٰى\nWA SABAATAN FIL HODAA\nsteadfastness in (the path of) guidance,\nوَ التَّوْفِيْقَ لِمَا تُحِبُّ وَ تَرْضٰى\nWAT TAWFEEQA LEMAA TOHIBBO WA TARZAA\nsuccess in what pleases and satisfies You,\nوَ رِزْقًا واسِعًا حَلَالًا طَيِّبًا\nWA RIZQAN WAASE-A’N HALAALAN TAYYEBAN\na sustenance that is vast, lawful, pure,\nمَرِيْئًا دَارًّا سَائِغًا\nMAREE-AN DAARRAN SAA-EGHAN\nadequate, fruitful, pleasant,\nفَاضِلًا مُفَضِّلًا صَبًّا صَبًّا\nFAAZELAN MOFAZZELAN SABBAN SABBAN\nabundant, superior, pouring forth,\nمِنْ غَيْرِ كَدٍّ وَ لَا نَكَدٍ وَ لَا مِنَّةٍ مِنْ اَحَدٍ\nMIN GHAYRE KADDIN WA LAA NAKADIN WA LAA MINNATIN MIN AHADIN\nwithout any toil, trouble, and favor from anyone.\nوَ عَافِيَةً مِنْ كُلِّ بَلَاءٍ وَ سُقْمٍ وَ مَرَضٍ\nWA A’AFEYATAN MIN KULLE BALAA-IN WA SUQMIN WA MARAZIN\nPreserve my health against any affliction, ailment, and disease,\nوَ الشُّكْرَ عَلَى الْعَافِيَةِ وَ النَّعْمَاءِ\nWASH SHUKRA A’LAL A’AFEYATE WAN NA’MAA-E\nGrant me appreciation of well-being and blessings,\nوَ اِذَا جَاءَ الْمَوْتُ فَاقْبِضْنَا عَلٰى اَحْسَنِ مَا يَكُوْنُ لَكَ طَاعَةً\nWA EZAA JAA-AL MAWTO FAQBIZNAA A’LAA AHSANE MAA YAKOONO LAKA TAA-A’TAN\nAnd when the time of death arrives, take our soul while it is in the best condition of obedience to You,\nعَلٰى مَا اَمَرْتَنَا مُحَافِظِيْنَ حَتّٰى تُؤَدِّيَنَا اِلٰى جَنَّاتِ النَّعِيْمِ\nA’LAA MAA AMARTANAA MOHAAFEZEENA HATTAA TO-ADDEYANAA ELAA JANNAATIN NA-E’EME\nAnd while observing what You commanded, so that You lead us to the Garden of blessings.\nبِرَحْمَتِكَ يَا اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِيْنَ\nBE-RAHMATEKA YAA ARHAMAR RAAHEMEENA\nBy Your mercy, O the most merciful of the merciful!\nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَ آلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLE A’LAA MOHAMMADIN WA AALE MOHAMMADIN\nMy Allah! Bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad,\nوَ اَوْحِشْنِيْ مِنَ الدُّنْيَا وَ آنِسْنِيْ بِالْآخِرَةِ\nWA AWHISH-NEE MENAD DUNYAA WA AANISNEE BIL-AAKHERATE\nand estrange me from (the attractions of) the world, and make me familiar with (the affairs of) the hereafter.\nفَاِنَّهٗ لَا يُوْحِشُ مِنَ الدُّنْيا اِلَّا خَوْفُكَ\nFA-INNAHU LAA YOOHESHO MENAD DUNYAA ILLAA KHAWFOKA\nCertainly, nothing causes alienation from this world except fear of You,\nوَ لَا يُؤْنِسُ بِالْآخِرَةِ اِلَّا رَجَآؤُكَ\nWA LAA YOANESO BIL-AAKHERATE ILLAA RAJAAA-OKA\nand nothing causes to be accustomed to the hereafter except hope for Your (mercy).\nاَللّٰهُمَّ لَكَ الْحُجَّةُ لَا عَلَيْكَ\nALLAAHUMMA LAKAL HUJJATO LAA A’LAYKA\nO Allah! For You is the argument, not against You,\nوَ اِلَيْكَ الْمُشْتَكٰى لَا مِنْكَ\nWA ELAYKAL MUSHTAKAA LAA MINKA\nand to You is complained, not from You.\nفَصَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَ آلِهٖ\nFA-SALLE A’LAA MOHAMMADIN WA AALEHI\nThus, bless Muhammad and his family,\nوَ اَعِنِّي عَلٰى نَفْسِيَ الظَّالِمَةِ الْعَاصِيَةِ\nWA A-I’NNEE A’LAA NAFSEYAZ ZAALEMATIL A’ASEYATE\nand assist me against my unjust and disobedient soul,\nوَ شَهْوَتِيَ الْغَالِبَةِ\nWA SHAWATEYAL GHAALEBATE\nand my dominant desire.\nوَاخْتِمْ لِيْ بِالْعَافِيَةِ\nWAKH TIM LEE BIL-A’AFEYATE\nAnd conclude me with a safe and healthy end.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنَّ اسْتِغْفَارِيْ اِيَّاكَ وَ اَنَا مُصِرٌّ عَلٰى مَانَهَيْتَ قِلَّةُ حَيَآءٍ\nALLAAHUMMA INNAS TIGHFAAREE IYYAAKA WA ANAA MOSIRRUN A’LAA MAA NAHAYTA QILLATO HAYAAA-IN\nO Allah! It is due to my shamelessness that I ask forgiveness while I insist on what You have forbidden.\nوَ تَرْكِيَ الْاِسْتِغْفَارَ مَعَ عِلْمِيْ بِسِعَةِ حِلْمِكَ تَضْيِيْعٌ لِحَقِّ الرَّجَآءِ\nWA TARKEYAL ISTEGHFAARA MA-A’ I’LMEE BE-SE-A’TE HILMEKA TAZ-YEE-U’N LEHAQQIR RAJAAA-E\nOn the other hand, if I do not ask for forgiveness with my knowledge of Your abundant forbearance, it will be wasting the right of hope (to You).\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنَّ ذُنُوْبِيْ تُؤْيِسُنِيْ اَنْ اَرْجُوَكَ\nALLAAHUMMA INNA ZONOOBEE TOAYESONEE AN ARJOWAKA\nMy Allah! (due to my weak faith) my sins discourage me from requesting You,\nوَ اِنَّ عِلْمِيْ بِسِعَةِ رَحْمَتِكَ يَمْنَعُنِيْ اَنْ اَخْشَاكَ\nWA INNA I’LMEE BE-SE-A’TE RAHMATEKA YAMNA-O’NEE AN AKHSAAKA\nand my knowledge about Your vast mercy prevents me from fearing You.\nفَصَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَ آلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nFA-SALLE A’LAA MOHAMMADIN WA AALE MOHAMMADIN\nThus, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad,\nوَ صَدِّقْ رَجَائِيْ لَكَ\nWA SADDIQ RAJAA-EE LAKA\nand confirm my hope in You,\nوَ كَذِّبْ خَوْفِيْ مِنْكَ\nWA KAZZIB KHAWFEE MINKA\nnegate my fear of You,\nوَ كُنْ لِيْ عِنْدَ اَحْسَنِ ظَنِّيْ بِكَ يَا اَكْرَمَ الْاَكْرَمِيْنَ\nWA KUN LEE I’NDA AHSANE ZANNEE BEKA YAA AKRAMAL AKRAMEENA\nand be for me according to the best of what I expect and believe about You, O the most generous of the generous!\nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَ آلِ مُحَمَّدٍ وَ اَيِّدْنِيْ بِالْعِصْمَةِ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLE A’LAA MOHAMMADIN WA AALE MOHAMMADIN WA AYYIDNEE BIL-I’SMATE\nO Allah! Bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, and support me by protection (from sins),\nوَ اَنْطِقْ لِسَانِيْ بِالْحِكْمَةِ\nWA ANTIQ LESAANEE BIL-HIKMATE\nMake my tongue speak wisdom,\nوَ اجْعَلْنِيْ مِمَّنْ يَنْدَمُ عَلٰى ما ضَيَّعَهٗ فِيْ اَمْسِهٖ\nWAJ A’LNEE MIMMAN YANDAMO A’LAA MAA ZAYYA-A’HU FEE AMSEHI\nPlace me among those who regret what they wasted yesterday,\nوَ لَا يَغْبَنُ حَظَّهٗ فِيْ يَوْمِهٖ\nWA LAA YAGHBANO HAZZAHU FEE YAWMEHI\ndo not aggrieve their portion today,\nوَ لَا يَهُمُّ لِرِزْقِ غَدِهٖ\nWA LAA YAHUMMO LE-RIZQE GHADEHI\nand do not worry about the sustenance of tomorrow.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنَّ الْغَنِيَّ مَنِ اسْتَغْنٰى بِكَ وَ افْتَقَرَ اِلَيْكَ\nALLAAHUMMA INNAL GHANIYYA MANIS TAGHNAA BEKA WAF TAQARA ELAYKA\nO Allah! Certainly, rich is he who suffices himself with You and considers himself in need of You,\nوَ الْفَقِيْرَ مَنِ اسْتَغْنٰى بِخَلْقِكَ عَنْكَ\nWAL FAQEERO MANIS TAGHNAA BE-KHALQEKA A’NKA\nand poor is he who feels that he can suffice himself through Your creation without You.\nفَصَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَ آلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nFA-SALLE A’LAA MOHAMMADIN WA AALE MOHAMMADIN\nThus, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad,\nوَ اَغْنِنْي عَنْ خَلْقِكَ بِكَ\nWA AGHNENEE A’N KHALQEKA BEKA\nand suffice me from Your creation by Yourself,\nوَ اجْعَلْنِيْ مِمَّنْ لَا يَبْسُطُ كَفًّا اِلَّا اِلَيْكَ\nWAJ A’LNEE MIMMAN LAA YABSOTO KAFFAN ILLAA ELAYKA\nand put me amongst those who do not extend their hand except towards You.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنَّ الشَّقِيَّ مَنْ قَنَطَ وَ اَمَامَهُ التَّوْبَةُ وَ وَرَآءَهُ الرَّحْمَةُ\nALLAAHUMMA INNASH SHAQIYYA MAN QANATA WA AMAAMAHUT TAWBATO WA WARAAA-AHUR RAHMATO\nMy Allah! Certainly, wretched is he who despairs while repentance is placed before him and mercy is after him,\nوَ اِنْ كُنْتُ ضَعِيْفَ الْعَمَلِ فَاِ نِّيْ فِيْ رَحْمَتِكَ قَوِيُّ الْاَمَلِ\nWA IN KUNTO ZA-E’EFAL A’MALE FA-INNEE FEE RAHMATEKA QAWIYYUL AMALE\nEven though I have been weak in action, I have strong hope in Your mercy, \nفَهَبْ لِيْ ضَعْفَ عَمَلِيْ لِقُوَّةِ اَمَلِيْ\nFA-HAB LEE ZA’FA A’MALEE LE-QUWWATE AMALEE\nThus, forgive the weakness of my action in light of the strength of my hope.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنْ كُنْتَ تَعْلَمُ اَنْ مَا فِيْ عِبَادِكَ مَنْ هُوَ اَقْسِىْ قَلْبًا مِنِّيْ وَ اَعْظَمُ مِنِّيْ ذَنْبًا\nALLAAHUMMA IN KUNTA TA’LAMO AN MAA FEE E’BAADEKA MAN HOWA AQSEE QALBAN MINNEE WA A-A’ZAMO MINNEE ZANBAN\nO Allah! Even if You know there is no one amongst Your servants with harder heart and greater sins than mine,\nفَاِ نِّيْ اَعْلَمُ اَنَّهٗ لَا مَوْلٰى اَعْظَمُ مِنْكَ طَوْلًا\nFA-INNEE A-A’LAMO ANNAHU LAA MAWLAA A-A’ZAMO MINKA TAWLAN\nI certainly know that there is no master more generous than You,\nوَ اَوْسَعُ رَحْمَةً وَ عَفْوًا\nWA AWSA-O’ RAHMATAN WA A’FWAN\nwith greater mercy and forgiveness.\nفَيَا مَنْ هُوَ اَوْحَدُ فِيْ رَحْمَتِهٖ\nFAYAA MAN HOWA AWHADO FEE RAHMATEHI\nThen, O He Who is unique in His mercy!\nاِغْفِرْ لِمَنْ لَيْسَ بِاَوْحَدَ فِيْ خَطِيْئَتِهٖ\nIGHFIR LEMAN LAYSA BE-AWHADA FEE KHATEE-ATEHI\nForgive him, who is not unique in his mistakes.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنَّكَ اَمَرْتَنَا فَعَصَيْنَا\nALLAAHUMMA INNAKA AMARTANAA FA-A’SAYNAA\nO Allah! Certainly, You commanded us, but we have disobeyed,\nوَ نَهَيْتَ فَمَا انْتَهَيْنَا\nWA NAHAYTA FAMAN TAHAYNAA\nforbade us, but we did not desist,\nوَ ذَكَّرْتَ فَتَنَاسَيْنَا\nWA ZAKKARTA FATANAASAYNAA\nreminded us, but we remained unmindful,\nوَ بَصَّرْتَ فَتَعَامَيْنَا\nWA BASSARTA FATA-A’AMAYNAA\nenlightened us, but we behaved blindly,\nوَ حَذَّرْتَ فَتَعَدَّيْنَا\nWA HAZZARTA FATA-A’DDAYNAA\nand warned us, but we transgressed.\nوَ مَا كَانَ ذٰلِكَ جَزَآءَ اِحْسَانِكَ اِلَيْنَا\nWA MAA KAANA ZAALEKA JAZAA-A EHSAANEKA ELAYNAA\nThis was not the repayment of Your kindness to us,\nوَ اَنْتَ اَعْلَمُ بِمَا اَعْلَنَّا وَ اَخْفَيْنَا\nWA ANTA A-A’LAMO BEMAA A-A’LANNAA WA AKHFAYNAA\nand You know what we have disclosed and have concealed,\nوَ اَخْبَرُ بِمَا نَأْتِيْ وَ مَا اَتَيْنَا\nWA AKHBARO BEMAA NAATEE WA MAA ATAYNAA\nand You are aware of what we will do and have done.\nفَصَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَ آلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nFASALLE A’LAA MOHAMMADIN WA AALE MOHAMMADIN\nThus, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad,\nوَ لَا تُؤَاخِذْنَا بِما اَخْطَأْنَا وَ نَسِيْنَا\nWA LAA TO-AAKHIZNAA BEMAA AKHTAANAA WA NASEENAA\nand pardon us for our mistakes and our forgetfulness, \nوَ هَبْ لَنَا حُقُوْقَكَ لَدَيْنَا\nWA HAB LANAA HOQOOQAKA LADAYNAA\nforgive us the negligence of Your rights by us,\nوَ اَتِمَّ اِحْسَانَكَ اِلَيْنَا\nWA ATIMMAA EHSAANAKA ELAYNAA\ncomplete Your beneficence towards us,\nوَ اَسْبِلْ رَحْمَتَكَ عَلَيْنَا\nWA ASBIL RAHMATAKA A’LAYNAA\nand cause Your mercy to descend upon us.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنَّا نَتَوَسَّلُ اِلَيْكَ بِهٰذَا الصِّدِّيْقِ الْاِمَامِ\nALLAAHUMMA INNAA NATAWASSALO ELAYKA BEHAAZAS SIDDEEQIL EMAAME\nMy Allah! We seek nearness to You by means of this truthful Imam,\nوَ نَسْئَلُكَ بِالْحَقِّ الَّذِيْ جَعَلْتَهٗ لَهٗ وَ لِجَدِّهٖ رَسُولِكَ وَ لِاَبَوَيْهِ عَلِيٍّ وَ فَاطِمَةَ اَهْلِ بَيْتِ الرَّحْمَةِ\nWA NAS-ALOKA BIL-HAQQIL LAZEE JA-A’LTAHU LAHU WA LE-JADDEHI RASOOLEKA WA LE-ABAWAYHE A’LIYYIN WA FAATEMATA AHLE BAYTIR RAHMATE\nand request You by the rights that You have placed for him, his grandfather, his parents, Ali and Fatima, the household of mercy,\nاِدْرَارَ الرِّزْقِ الَّذِيْ بِهٖ قِوَامُ حَيَاتِنَا وَ صَلَاحُ اَحْوَالِ عِيَالِنَا\nIDRAARAR RIZQIL LAZEE BEHI QEWAAMO HAYAATENAA WA SALAAHO AHWAALE E’YAALENAA\nan abundant flow of livelihood that maintains our life and the welfare of our dependents.\nفَاَنْتَ الْكَرِيْمُ الَّذِيْ تُعْطِيْ مِنْ سِعَةٍ\nFA-ANTAL KAREEMUL LAZEE TO’TEE MIN SE-A’TE\nCertainly You are the generous one who grants abundantly,\nوَ تَمْنَعُ مِنْ قُدْرَةٍ\nWA TAMNA-O’ MIN QUDRATIN\nand holds back having power (to fulfill).\nوَ نَحْنُ نَسْئَلُكَ مِنَ الرِّزْقِ مايَكُوْنُ صَلَاحًا لِلدُّنْيا وَ بَلَاغًا لِلْآخِرَةِ\nWA NAHNO NASALOKA MENAR RIZQE MAA YAKOONO SALAAHAN LID-DUNYAA WA BALAAGHAN LIL-AAKHERATE\nWe request from You a livelihood that brings the goodness of this world and the pleasure of the hereafter,\nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَ آلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLE A’LAA MOHAMMADIN WA AALE MOHAMMADIN\nO Allah! Bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad,\nوَ اغْفِرْلَنَا وَ لِوالِدَيْنَا\nWAGH FIR LANAA WA LE-WAALEDAYNAA\nand forgive me, my parents,\nوَ لِجَمِيْعِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ وَ الْمُؤْمِنَاتِ\nWA LE-JAMEE-I’L MOAMENEENA WAL MOAMENAATE\nall the believing men and women,\nوَالْمُسْلِمِيْنَ وَ الْمُسْلِمَاتِ\nWAL MUSLEMEENA WAL MUSLEMAATE\nand the submissive men and women,\nاَلْاَحْيَآءِ مِنْهُمْ وَ الْاَمْوَاتِ\nAL-AHYAAA-E MINHUM WAL AMWAATE\nthe living of them and the dead.\nوَ آتِنَا فِي الدُّنْيَا حَسَنَةً وَ فِي الْآخِرَةِ حَسَنَةً وَ قِنَا عَذَابَ النَّارِ.\nWA AATENAA FID DUNYAA HASANATAN WA FIL AAKHERATE HASANATAN WA QENAA A’ZAABAN NAARE.\nGive us good in this world and good in the hereafter, and shield us from the torment of the fire.\nThen, complete your prayer, and recite Tasbihat (of Lady Fatima (a.s.)), and then place the side of you face on the ground and say the following forty times:\nسُبْحانَ اللهِ وَ الْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ وَ لَا اِلٰهَ اِلاَّ اللهُ وَ اللهُ اَكْبَرُ\nSUBHAANAL LAAHE WAL HAMDO LILLAAHE WA LAA ELAAHA ILLAL LAAHO WAL LAAHO AKBARO\nGlory be to Allah! Praise be to Allah! There is no deity but Allah! Allah is greater (than being described).\nFollowing that, ask Allah for protection, salvation, forgiveness, success in performing good deeds, and the acceptance of the actions that you do to seek His nearness and perform for His sake.\nThen, embrace the inner shrine, kiss it, and say:\nزَادَ اللهُ فِيْ شَرَفِكُمْ وَ السَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ وَ رَحْمَةُ اللهِ وَ بَرَكاتُهٗ.\nZAADAL LAAHO FEE SHARAFEKUM WAS SALAAMO A’ALAYKUM WA RAHMATUL LAAHE WA BARAKAATOHU.\nMay Allah increase your honor. Peace be upon you, the mercy of Allah, and His blessings.\nFinally, pray for yourself, your parents and for whomever else you wish.\nImam Mahdi (a.s.) said,\n“I pray for any believer who remembers the sufferings of my martyred grandfather, al-Husain (a.s.), and then prays for my relief (al-Faraj)”"
